WEBVTT

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:36.480
In the decades after mankind's swollen population began overflowing into outer space,

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:40.240
hundreds of gigantic colonies were constructed in Earth's orbit.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.910
Within their cylindrical walls, man tried to recreate his old environment

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:50.190
as a new homeland for the human race. Generations were born, lived and died

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.070
within these man-made worlds.

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:57.140
Here they thrived in peaceful contentment until the year 0079 of the

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.610
Universal Century.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:17.830
Having bestowed upon themselves the title of the Duchy of Zion, the colonies of the furthest outside orbit, known as Side 3, launched a war of independence against the Federated Union of Earth.

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:24.480
Mankind was horrified as the first month of fighting saw both sides lose half of their populations.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:29.600
The bitter carnage has raged on for eight months with no resolution in sight.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.560
Under these unthinkable nightmare conditions,

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:45.200
the continuing existence of humankind itself is very much in question.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:59.800
"All clear. Their military headquarters are set up in Sector 19. Nothing's stirring though. No troops inside anywhere. There's no activity anywhere. It's like a ghost town. Except for that one young kid."

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:06.070
Amaro!

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:07.090
What?

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:08.070
He hasn't even eaten yet.

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:09.230
Amaro!

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:17.990
You spend every minute of your life working.

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:20.100
You won't even take time off for breakfast.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.100
That's not healthy.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:21.950
You know?

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:23.450
Good morning, Amaro.

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:25.450
You're looking very well today.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:27.450
And you look fine as always, Haro.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:28.280
Do I really?

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:30.000
Thank you.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.000
What are you gonna wear?

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:31.930
We have to hurry.

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:33.170
Amaro!

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:35.040
I'll eat once I finish this, Frau.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.040
I'll just be a minute.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:38.040
Didn't you get the orders of evacuation?

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.000
You say we're evacuating?

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.000
I wondered why they were blowing the sirens.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:45.000
Oh, honestly, Amaro, don't you listen to the army broadcasts?

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.000
We're ordered to move to the bomb shelter.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.000
A warship was sent to protect us.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.000
Just a sec.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.000
I'm trying to concentrate.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.000
Will you stop fooling around, Amaro?

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.000
Come on!

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:56.000
All right already, all right!

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.750
Get dressed quickly while I wait outside.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:00.000
Give me a break.

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:03.990
Wait a minute, Hayato!

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:06.670
Huh? We've got to get out of here, Frau Bo.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:09.650
Why didn't you tell Amuro about the army's evacuation orders?

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:11.290
You know he's living all alone there.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:13.150
Well, why didn't his genius daddy tell him?

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:14.770
Hey, why so hostile, Hayato?

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:20.110
Well, his father and the other scientists create nothing but trouble in that fancy research center.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:23.250
I can understand why you're mad at the government for making us move out,

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:24.550
but it's all for the war effort.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.790
It isn't just the research center I'm mad about.

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:27.390
Hurry, son!

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:29.100
Okay. Bye!

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:29.480
Bye!

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:35.990
Look at you, I guess that's what you call breakfast.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:43.800
Do you think your dad might be on that warship that's coming in from Earth today?

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:44.800
I sure hope so.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:47.630
He's been Earthside for a whole week now and I'm running out of money.

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:50.130
Do you think our colony will get caught up in the war?

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:51.030
How would I know?

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:53.240
Besides, I never get any news out of my father.

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:11.310
Tell the ground crew to get moving! I want those Gundam parts loaded on White Base now, not sometime next week!

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:12.500
Aye, aye, Commander.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:16.860
Damn White Base anyway. They let a Zeke ship trail them here and put all of us in jeopardy.

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:20.480
So that's our new mobile suit carrier, huh?

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:20.960
Yeah.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:24.750
She is very impressive. She's gonna be a hell of a ship once they work the bugs out.

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:30.000
Once White Base and the Gundam start showing off their true capabilities, those Zeons won't stand a chance against us.

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:49.790
Lieutenant Ray, we've just about completed our docking operations with Side 7, sir.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:51.830
Will you be joining us at the bridge now?

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:53.990
Yes, I will, Ensign. Thank you.

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:55.410
Your name's Bright, isn't it?

00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:56.010
Yes, sir.

00:06:56.570 --> 00:06:58.930
How long have you been in the military service, Ensign Bright?

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:00.000
Six months.

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:03.760
I hope we can get Gundam into action right away.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:08.120
I want to end this war before young men like you have to get involved in actual combat.

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:09.600
Is that your son, Lieutenant?

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:15.510
Yes. I understand boys his age are now forming guerrilla bands.

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:16.990
That can't be true.

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:19.320
I have heard those stories, sir. I believe they're true.

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:19.980
It must end.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:22.480
At ease, Lieutenant Gray.

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:24.960
Sir, I understand we were being followed by a Zeon ship.

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:26.720
Were we able to throw it off our trail?

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:28.510
No, Lieutenant. We couldn't lose him.

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:30.000
That's very unfortunate.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:41.590
That's three mobile suits that have come out, and we have to assume there are more inside.

00:07:41.590 --> 00:07:43.930
There's no time to spare! We have to hit 'em now!

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:46.320
You heard the orders. We're only here for surveillance.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.930
So do we just stand here and let 'em start filling the whole carrier up with those things?

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:53.740
I don't want to see any heroics. This isn't the time for it.

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:55.090
Gene, come back here!

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:56.760
I'll be famous like Shaw!

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:30.000
big mistake. If I carry this off, then you're going to be taking orders from me. The only

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.040
purpose of war is to destroy your enemies.

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:41.420
What was that? I don't know.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:42.860
It sounded like something blew up.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.300
Something inside the colony? What could that be?

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:47.340
Oh, no. We must have

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:49.000
fallen under a Zeon sneak attack.

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:50.280
We'll be sitting ducks.

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:55.340
Don't anyone panic. We have our army

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:57.510
to protect us. Where are you going?

00:08:57.750 --> 00:08:59.050
I've got to look for my father.

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:00.000
Amuro?

00:09:00.380 --> 00:09:02.580
Don't open that door, boy. You're gonna get us all in trouble.

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:04.880
This shelter capsule won't hold up under heavy fire.

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:08.080
I'll ask permission to evacuate to that carrier or the doctor today.

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:10.070
We'll die if we stay here.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:11.130
Huh?

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:12.630
Wait! Don't open that!

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:15.840
Seal the passageway and stay inside.

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:23.770
I'd heard about those active robots, but I didn't believe it.

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:29.800
Have the Xeons deployed an army of Roboton invaders?

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:39.260
All civilians are supposed to be in the shelter capsules!

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:41.840
My father is Dr. Ray. He's working as an army scientist.

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:43.260
Do you know where he might be found?

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:46.180
He should be on the ship. You get back to the shelter, young man.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:47.220
Huh?

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:48.040
Look at that, kid!

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:48.480
Huh?

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:50.000
Whoa!

00:10:18.940 --> 00:10:19.660
It's a nightmare.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:24.960
Classified material, top secret.

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:27.120
Weapons Department of the Federal Forces.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:28.450
Mobile suit?

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:29.260
What?

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:40.700
schematic and complete operations manual model experimental gundam told me to stay in the

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:46.390
construction area in case anything went wrong i obeyed all right just tell me where denim is now

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:50.470
oh well he went out with jeans so he could supervise his surveillance are you absolutely

00:10:50.470 --> 00:10:54.930
certain the federal forces brought mobile suits yes sir continue the surveillance and get all the

00:10:54.930 --> 00:11:00.000
photographs you can but if the action gets too hot get out of there yes sir orders understood what happened

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:07.130
young slender thinks he's a hero and he can't be controlled so now i have to take over surveillance

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:20.940
take us a little closer to side seven sir all the movements are coordinated by computer

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:30.000
well now i see what dad was so excited about we have to get on board the world

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:31.290
We have to hurry.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:49.510
Go on to the spaceport and wait there, frow!

00:11:49.510 --> 00:11:50.510
Elmero!

00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:55.080
Dad! I'm coming to help!

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:59.160
He can't send me back home anyway.

00:12:04.350 --> 00:12:06.150
We have to save the people first!

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:09.200
Get a shelter right now!

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:11.650
Dad, we have to save the people first.

00:12:11.810 --> 00:12:13.410
They're more important than any machine is.

00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:14.410
Let's get started.

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:15.550
We're under attack.

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:17.820
Get aboard White Base immediately, Amaro.

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:19.060
White Base? What is that?

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:21.100
The military ship I came here in.

00:12:21.530 --> 00:12:22.510
What's the hold up here?

00:12:22.610 --> 00:12:24.330
The starter's dead. It won't turn over.

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:26.700
Amaro, get on board now!

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:28.310
I'll try to find a tractor.

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:30.000
But I wanted to help.

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:34.970
One thing for sure, Gundam.

00:12:35.110 --> 00:12:37.110
You're big enough, but how bad are you?

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:39.070
Better than the Zaku?

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:41.080
I wonder if...

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:06.510
Can you hear me, Frau? Can you stand? Do you think anything's broken?

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:09.120
No. What about you?

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:10.080
I'm okay.

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:13.680
Oh, no. I see them, and they aren't moving.

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:16.150
Who, Frau? Who do you see?

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:21.070
Father. Grandfather.

00:13:34.510 --> 00:13:42.410
I'm so sorry, Frau.

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:44.250
We have to get out of here now.

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:45.490
We don't want to get captured.

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:48.530
Come on, get control of it!

00:13:48.710 --> 00:13:50.570
You mustn't fall apart on me now!

00:13:53.590 --> 00:13:55.730
You have to get aboard the White Base.

00:13:56.180 --> 00:13:57.460
Think you can get there without me?

00:13:58.120 --> 00:13:59.860
I'll know you're safe there.

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:01.010
I'll find dad.

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:03.340
I'll join you as soon as possible.

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:04.880
I think I can make it.

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:06.020
You can do it.

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:07.130
You can do it.

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:14.100
Frau, I'm sorry.

00:14:14.550 --> 00:14:15.740
I have work to do.

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:17.470
I have to join the fight.

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:37.620
They left this thing turned on.

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:39.090
I hope I can do this.

00:14:39.090 --> 00:14:40.240
I have to try.

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:47.140
No sweat.

00:14:47.140 --> 00:14:50.840
Just have to follow the instructions.

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:53.790
Wow, it's amazing.

00:14:53.790 --> 00:14:56.580
There's practically unlimited energy powering this thing.

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:57.810
I think I can handle it.

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:13.010
what's next uh-huh and now i can open the visors uh-oh

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:30.000
you want your core fighter we'd have to blast through the side do we have all available combat personnel out there

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:30.960
Yes, sir.

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:34.220
Ah, by attacking from the inside, they caught us off guard.

00:15:34.220 --> 00:15:39.830
Hey! Better get this thing on its feet!

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:43.180
Uh-oh! He saw me!

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:45.920
Oh no! What do I do?

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:49.900
Fire!

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:55.710
Possible! This was a shipment of parts. They couldn't assemble a complete unit that quickly.

00:15:55.710 --> 00:15:57.110
What are you talking about?

00:15:57.110 --> 00:15:59.890
Every unit has to be disassembled before shipping.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:13.640
- The pilot's having a lot of trouble with it.

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:15.850
Our lasers didn't even put a scratch on it.

00:16:15.850 --> 00:16:17.270
What the hell's that thing made of anyway?

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:25.730
- I've got it now, move, come on!

00:16:25.730 --> 00:16:27.180
- Fight, we're on reconnaissance.

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:28.450
Come on, we're pulling out.

00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:30.000
We gotta stop him here and now.

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:31.190
never have an opportunity

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:32.070
like this again.

00:16:33.030 --> 00:16:33.990
Do as I say.

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:38.400
Real easy.

00:16:39.530 --> 00:16:39.990
Okay.

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:41.900
Balance gyro is running.

00:16:43.030 --> 00:16:43.470
Yeah.

00:16:58.980 --> 00:17:00.000
It looks to me like one of our

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:04.380
mobile suits has come to life on its own. Have I gone crazy?

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:08.910
I don't know who's in that cockpit, but he doesn't know much about combat.

00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:12.020
Don't tell me I've run out of ammunition already.

00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:16.060
I'm dead. I got him now. Leave it to me, sir. It's gonna be my pleasure.

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:21.910
Huh? I'm a goner.

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:29.760
Sorry. I'm afraid I'm gonna have to reduce you to a pile of scrap metal.

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:06.810
Huh?

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:08.130
I need a weapon.

00:18:08.130 --> 00:18:11.440
But I don't even know what I'm looking for, let alone where to find it.

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:12.930
Laser swords.

00:18:12.930 --> 00:18:19.110
You can make it out to the camp by yourself. I'll hold it down.

00:18:19.110 --> 00:18:21.540
I think I can still make a jet jump if you give me a boost.

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:23.350
And once I'm airborne, I'll be all right.

00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:24.890
I'll give it full power!

00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:26.120
Oh, no you don't!

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:08.130
"Wow, I've already ripped open the outside of the bulkhead. The base itself could tear apart. I mustn't fire the cannon. How am I gonna defend myself?"

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:12.210
"You're gonna be sorry you were ever born!"

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:23.810
"If the fuel tank gets hit, the blast would blow out the remaining oxygen. I have to disable the central control system. My aim has to be perfect!"

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:04.000
Get those civilians aboard the white base!

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:04.980
Go ahead.

00:20:04.980 --> 00:20:07.770
The leak in the bulkhead has been completely sealed now, sir.

00:20:07.770 --> 00:20:09.470
And how's the Gundam transfer going?

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:13.570
Afraid we've lost all of our engineers, sir, and nobody else here knows how to operate those things.

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:15.270
Then we'll have to rely on him.

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:16.440
What, sir?

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:18.940
I don't think he's a real pilot, but he knows what he's doing.

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:21.040
That puts him a step ahead of everyone else.

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:23.720
At any rate, he's the only defense we have.

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:26.020
Incoming missile? Where'd it come from?

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:40.620
What happened to Slender?

00:20:40.620 --> 00:20:42.800
- He managed to escape from side seven.

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:44.400
He fought his way back to the ship.

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:46.450
- I hope he learns from his mistakes.

00:20:46.450 --> 00:20:48.260
He'll have to be reprimanded.

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:55.770
But we all made errors like that when we were young.

00:20:55.770 --> 00:21:00.000
- We need some help up here, quick, order some of those

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.920
civilians to volunteer.

00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:05.990
Incoming duck and cover!

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:21.890
Missiles came from outside.

00:21:21.890 --> 00:21:23.890
I'm okay, look for the children!

00:21:23.890 --> 00:21:25.890
Rob, what happened? You'll have to get aboard whitebaits right now!

00:21:25.890 --> 00:21:27.890
This isn't happening!

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:28.890
Grab hold of the bar!

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:44.580
Whoa, and its voice sounded an awful lot like Amaro's. Is that possible?

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:50.590
Get out of here, frown. You'll be-

00:21:50.590 --> 00:21:57.900
Captain! You have to get back to the ship. The crew needs you. I can take over here.

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:00.000
You haven't had any training as a gunner. Can you-

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.000
I learned quick, sir!

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:04.000
Good enough!

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:09.430
Okay, sir!

00:22:09.430 --> 00:22:11.540
Fine, but I need a hand getting down!

00:22:11.540 --> 00:22:17.560
Now! Yes, sir. Right away, sir!

00:22:17.560 --> 00:22:19.560
Sir! I realize you were trying to show initiative,

00:22:19.560 --> 00:22:21.560
but you went too far, and while I won't punish you this time,

00:22:21.560 --> 00:22:23.560
I don't want to see that happen again.

00:22:23.560 --> 00:22:25.560
I learned a lesson, sir, I promise!

00:22:25.560 --> 00:22:27.770
I still find it hard to believe that the Fettys

00:22:27.770 --> 00:22:30.000
could build such an incredibly powerful ship as you

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:30.780
you described to us.

00:22:30.800 --> 00:22:33.560
I can understand that, sir, but I didn't just imagine that thing.

00:22:33.580 --> 00:22:33.800
Right.

00:22:34.280 --> 00:22:34.600
Doran?

00:22:34.680 --> 00:22:34.880
Sir!

00:22:35.760 --> 00:22:39.940
Open a laser communications channel at once, and contact Admiral Dozel personally.

00:22:40.180 --> 00:22:43.540
You've had a very rough day, but we made it to the ship, and we'll be safe now.

00:22:43.560 --> 00:22:43.980
Hey, you!

00:22:44.140 --> 00:22:44.380
Me?

00:22:44.660 --> 00:22:46.080
Let the older folks watch the kids.

00:22:46.120 --> 00:22:48.280
We have a lot of wounded up here, and we can use your help.

00:22:48.480 --> 00:22:49.000
I'm coming!

00:22:49.440 --> 00:22:50.740
Don't anybody wander away.

00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:52.860
When I find your parents, I'll tell them where you are.

00:22:53.420 --> 00:22:54.710
Go right in there.

00:22:54.950 --> 00:22:55.270
Right.

00:22:55.980 --> 00:22:56.620
I'm here to help.

00:22:56.820 --> 00:22:57.440
What do I do?

00:22:57.440 --> 00:22:58.670
You can help me bandage.

00:22:58.770 --> 00:22:59.470
Get in the suture tank.

00:22:59.490 --> 00:23:00.000
Right away.

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:03.330
Start with the bandages on his side.

00:23:03.610 --> 00:23:04.830
Tape the top and bottom edges.

00:23:05.890 --> 00:23:09.210
If the Xeon ship has stopped firing,

00:23:09.350 --> 00:23:11.410
put your crews back to work reloading immediately.

00:23:11.550 --> 00:23:11.710
Sure.

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:13.350
Put the lieutenant in charge.

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:14.650
I need you on white base.

00:23:16.090 --> 00:23:17.970
Side 7 is totally wiped out.

00:23:18.270 --> 00:23:18.650
Oh, no.

00:23:19.080 --> 00:23:20.170
How bad is it, sir?

00:23:20.600 --> 00:23:22.340
All our defense team was annihilated

00:23:22.340 --> 00:23:24.440
before we had a chance to form a fighting posture.

00:23:24.600 --> 00:23:25.840
Our army's been decimated.

00:23:26.860 --> 00:23:29.170
I'm afraid we lost all of our engineers as well.

00:23:29.270 --> 00:23:30.000
The assembly area

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:35.830
took a missile hit. Those two Zakus have put us out of business. Our army has been reduced

00:23:35.830 --> 00:23:39.350
to seven soldiers and every one of them has been wounded seriously.

00:23:39.350 --> 00:23:42.970
Ensure all Gundam-related material is loaded on board immediately.

00:23:42.970 --> 00:23:47.850
Yes, sir. Fortunately, there's one Gundam pilot left and his unit is in ready condition,

00:23:47.850 --> 00:23:50.710
so he can help us with the on-loading and the reassembly operation.

00:23:50.710 --> 00:23:52.660
Does anybody know who that pilot is?

00:23:52.660 --> 00:23:54.660
His identity isn't on the pilot roster.

00:23:54.660 --> 00:23:58.380
Well, the minute he's finished transferring those materials, you'd better have White Base

00:23:58.380 --> 00:24:00.000
all set to launch right away.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:06.180
We can be ready to be out of sight seven in minutes set the controls on computer debarkation who takes over from there on

00:24:06.180 --> 00:24:09.180
I may speak sir. I'm only licensed for cruisers

00:24:09.180 --> 00:24:13.620
But I've memorized every word of the white base manual, and I'm sure I can handle it really and who are you?

00:24:13.980 --> 00:24:18.260
Forgive me. My name is Yashima Mirai, sir. Well

00:24:18.930 --> 00:24:21.810
Family is very well known

00:24:21.810 --> 00:24:24.050
I had planned a formal dinner for our officers tonight

00:24:24.050 --> 00:24:29.060
In which I was going to honor you and toast the successful completion of your mission, but you have wasted so much time

00:24:29.060 --> 00:24:30.000
I've had to cancel

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.000
All my invitations!

00:24:31.000 --> 00:24:34.740
Admiral Dozel, I have something more important to report to you.

00:24:34.740 --> 00:24:35.740
We found the V-Project.

00:24:35.740 --> 00:24:36.740
The V-Project?

00:24:36.740 --> 00:24:37.820
Yes, sir.

00:24:37.820 --> 00:24:41.260
It's the heart of their defense system, a gigantic research center and mobile suit production

00:24:41.260 --> 00:24:43.020
facility located on Side 7.

00:24:43.020 --> 00:24:44.610
Ah!

00:24:44.610 --> 00:24:46.610
I see why they call you Shah of the Red Comet!

00:24:46.610 --> 00:24:47.530
My congratulations!

00:24:47.530 --> 00:24:49.260
So, anything else?

00:24:49.260 --> 00:24:52.340
We were near the end of our mission, so we had very few missiles left, and we've used

00:24:52.340 --> 00:24:53.450
them all up, sir.

00:24:53.450 --> 00:24:54.780
Resupplied it once.

00:24:54.780 --> 00:24:56.690
Oh, one more thing, Admiral.

00:24:56.690 --> 00:24:58.570
We'll be needing three more Zakus as well, sir.

00:24:58.570 --> 00:25:00.000
I cannot believe what I'm hearing!

00:25:00.160 --> 00:25:06.060
That's right. Two of them were destroyed by a single mobile suit that was produced at the research laboratory.

00:25:06.060 --> 00:25:06.890
V-Project.

00:25:06.890 --> 00:25:10.990
All right, you'll get your Saku's. I want all the information you can get on the V-Project.

00:25:10.990 --> 00:25:13.990
Capture that mobile suit and send it to me as well.

00:25:13.990 --> 00:25:14.910
Yes, sir.

00:25:14.910 --> 00:25:15.910
Don't fail me, Shah.

00:25:15.910 --> 00:25:16.910
Sir.

00:25:16.910 --> 00:25:20.120
Lieutenant, I want three Class A Shock Troopers ready to move out immediately.

00:25:20.120 --> 00:25:24.120
Sir, won't you wait until the Ordnance Ship arrives to resupply us?

00:25:24.120 --> 00:25:28.020
Whenever possible, I use the element of surprise to keep a step ahead of my enemy.

00:25:28.020 --> 00:25:30.000
Slender slipped out of sight.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:34.380
7. That tells me. There must be a way for me to slip back in.

00:25:34.380 --> 00:25:48.210
What did you say that pilot's name was? Amuro, sir.

00:25:48.210 --> 00:25:52.150
I'm sure he wasn't one of my pilots. I guess he could be a test pilot from the

00:25:52.150 --> 00:25:56.100
Site 7 Research Center, sir. The communications board's on portside.

00:25:56.100 --> 00:26:00.000
Hail the Gundam so we can talk to him. Aye, aye, sir. Tell Amuro his orders are to

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:04.870
fly cover for us as we clear port. I don't know this board, sir. Where's the channel control?

00:26:05.230 --> 00:26:09.390
Where's the comm channel control, Miss Mirai? Red dial, upper right-hand corner of the console,

00:26:09.610 --> 00:26:14.620
sir. It's labeled channel control. Captain, this so-called pilot on board Gundam is just a kid.

00:26:15.080 --> 00:26:19.920
What? Nonsense. See for yourself, Captain. I know it sounds crazy, but he's just a young boy. He

00:26:19.920 --> 00:26:24.910
can't possibly be a pilot. He's not just any boy, sir. What do you know about him, Mirai? Amuro

00:26:24.910 --> 00:26:28.970
takes after his father, one of the most brilliant engineers on the Federation's mobile suit project.

00:26:29.070 --> 00:26:30.000
Tell me the truth now, boy.

00:26:30.030 --> 00:26:35.270
Did you really bring down two Zakus by yourself? All the credit really belongs to the Gundam. I was just along for the ride

00:26:35.270 --> 00:26:42.330
How did you get in there? Hold on, I recognize that voice. You're the ensign who ordered me to load all Gundam related materials aboard White Base

00:26:42.330 --> 00:26:47.910
Don't worry sir, I'll teach that kid a lesson. Take it easy, Brighton. Maybe he's the only pilot we have left

00:26:47.910 --> 00:26:57.080
I'll check out the laboratories. You search the residential block. Gotcha! Now, come on chief. I'm not gonna let you check out on me, you hear?

00:26:57.280 --> 00:27:00.000
Get back on board! Captain's orders, we've been sent

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:02.000
and make a last minute search for stragglers.

00:27:02.000 --> 00:27:04.890
Huh? Hey, were any others left behind?

00:27:04.890 --> 00:27:06.890
How would I know? I barely made it out in time myself.

00:27:06.890 --> 00:27:09.890
I didn't wait around to look for the lost, lame, or lazy.

00:27:09.890 --> 00:27:10.890
Hold the elevator.

00:27:10.890 --> 00:27:11.890
Well, come on, move it.

00:27:11.890 --> 00:27:12.890
What?

00:27:12.890 --> 00:27:17.930
What? Hey! Are you crazy?

00:27:17.930 --> 00:27:20.930
You're the most cowardly and disgusting person in the world.

00:27:20.930 --> 00:27:22.930
Hey, what's your problem, blondie?

00:27:22.930 --> 00:27:26.940
My problem is I shocked myself by wishing that we could just take off and leave you here.

00:27:26.940 --> 00:27:30.000
Well, who named you queen of the universe? You need to be taken down.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:35.350
a peg. I might just be the man for the job. Big man, I only wish I had the time to stay

00:27:35.350 --> 00:27:41.690
here and beat your tiny brains out. Let's go. Right. Okay, sweetheart. Give me a hand

00:27:41.690 --> 00:27:46.390
here. All right, all right. Hmm.

00:28:03.000 --> 00:28:08.640
Steer 8 degrees starboard, reduce ion reversal thrust to 5%, activate mega-particle cannons

00:28:08.640 --> 00:28:10.560
and stand by to fire on command.

00:28:10.560 --> 00:28:13.860
Target side 7 space gate, avoid the landing dock.

00:28:13.860 --> 00:28:17.120
Fire!

00:28:30.510 --> 00:28:31.750
I've done better myself.

00:28:31.750 --> 00:28:34.390
What's the best way in?

00:28:34.390 --> 00:28:37.370
This maintenance airlock accesses the environment shell, sir.

00:28:37.370 --> 00:28:38.350
Good.

00:28:38.350 --> 00:28:39.460
Move in.

00:28:39.460 --> 00:28:40.460
They're bombing the space gate.

00:28:40.460 --> 00:28:44.300
Sir, have you decided yet what we're going to do with this kid armor row?

00:28:44.300 --> 00:28:46.560
Can you identify who that is bombing us?

00:28:46.560 --> 00:28:50.360
Sir, I've just sighted a single Musai-class warship 40 degrees to port.

00:28:50.360 --> 00:28:51.800
It's closing on us rapidly!

00:28:51.800 --> 00:28:52.690
What?

00:28:52.690 --> 00:28:57.460
Notify everyone to destroy and jettison all unneeded Gundam parts and shred the documentation

00:28:57.460 --> 00:29:00.000
and issue a beam rifle to the Gundam.

00:29:00.320 --> 00:29:02.810
I don't want to send a boy into combat.

00:29:02.810 --> 00:29:06.950
I have no choice, though, and too many lives depend on the results of this action.

00:29:08.900 --> 00:29:10.440
I understand, Captain.

00:29:10.440 --> 00:29:15.450
Amuro, you've been assigned to pilot the Gundam and to destroy the loading dock on Side 7 at once.

00:29:15.450 --> 00:29:17.890
Sir, there are three mobile suits still left there!

00:29:17.890 --> 00:29:20.010
Right, and we don't want them falling into enemy hands!

00:29:20.010 --> 00:29:22.290
Excuse me, sir. The enemy ship is now standing off.

00:29:22.290 --> 00:29:25.260
Falling back? Now's our chance if we move fast!

00:29:25.260 --> 00:29:28.700
I think the quickest way to wipe out the loading dock is napalm spray.

00:29:28.700 --> 00:29:29.670
Okay, sir.

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:32.500
He even knows how to choose the perfect kind of weapon.

00:29:32.500 --> 00:29:34.300
The boy's got adult judgment.

00:29:34.300 --> 00:29:34.800
Ah!

00:29:34.800 --> 00:29:36.210
Final call for evacuation!

00:29:36.210 --> 00:29:43.210
I'm going to Amaro's to play, Mom!

00:29:43.210 --> 00:29:45.410
All right, darling, but don't be late for dinner!

00:29:45.410 --> 00:29:51.170
Anyone who's left, you must evacuate!

00:29:51.170 --> 00:29:56.180
It's like a graveyard.

00:29:56.180 --> 00:29:57.540
Hey!

00:30:13.120 --> 00:30:15.600
- Make a move, freeze!

00:30:15.600 --> 00:30:19.340
- Drop that right now!

00:30:19.340 --> 00:30:20.640
- Well, you certainly don't look

00:30:20.640 --> 00:30:22.280
like a typical soldier or gorilla.

00:30:22.280 --> 00:30:23.400
Who are you?

00:30:23.400 --> 00:30:28.070
- If I were you, I would stop.

00:30:28.070 --> 00:30:30.000
- Well now, I'm waiting for your command.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:31.980
Why does it seem like we've met before?

00:30:32.320 --> 00:30:34.360
Take off that stupid mask and show me your face.

00:30:42.120 --> 00:30:47.920
Little Artesia?

00:30:48.530 --> 00:30:49.170
It can't be.

00:30:49.230 --> 00:30:50.030
It just can't be.

00:30:52.700 --> 00:30:53.240
A Zeon?

00:30:53.540 --> 00:30:54.500
What is going on?

00:30:54.970 --> 00:30:55.670
Big Brother!

00:31:04.570 --> 00:31:06.530
It was him, I know it was.

00:31:06.880 --> 00:31:10.240
I have ordered everything on the loading dock with Super Napalm.

00:31:10.370 --> 00:31:11.270
I'll take you to safety.

00:31:11.490 --> 00:31:12.530
Climb up on my head.

00:31:13.570 --> 00:31:16.390
Don't worry, I can pick up an egg without breaking the shell.

00:31:16.510 --> 00:31:17.450
You're going to be just fine.

00:31:17.820 --> 00:31:19.380
Amuro, you haven't called in a report.

00:31:19.480 --> 00:31:20.100
What's going on?

00:31:20.180 --> 00:31:21.380
Just a minute, Mr. Bright.

00:31:21.670 --> 00:31:23.400
All set?

00:31:23.660 --> 00:31:23.960
Go!

00:31:37.420 --> 00:31:40.340
Captain! That Zeon slipped on board when he opened the gangway.

00:31:40.340 --> 00:31:41.440
We have an intruder!

00:31:41.440 --> 00:31:45.860
Ah, seal the section hatches and issue rifles to anybody who knows how to use one.

00:31:46.770 --> 00:31:49.610
Attention white base crew! We have a Zeon intruder!

00:31:49.610 --> 00:31:51.870
Shoot him first and ask questions afterwards!

00:31:51.870 --> 00:31:53.400
Aha!

00:32:05.560 --> 00:32:07.260
Prepare to debark immediately!

00:32:07.260 --> 00:32:14.140
He got my camera!

00:32:14.140 --> 00:32:27.880
Spotted me, move out!

00:32:55.720 --> 00:32:58.110
I have to fire, he's my enemy!

00:32:58.110 --> 00:32:59.190
Now fire!

00:33:02.300 --> 00:33:03.170
Select their mobile suit.

00:33:03.570 --> 00:33:05.350
Doran, arm two Zakus to the maximum.

00:33:05.540 --> 00:33:07.070
Send them out to Slender and me at once.

00:33:07.710 --> 00:33:08.630
We're prepared, sir.

00:33:08.690 --> 00:33:11.250
The Zakus are already standing by, ready to launch.

00:33:12.460 --> 00:33:13.700
Attention, Launch Bay 1.

00:33:14.200 --> 00:33:16.840
Program Zakus for course RD-23 and release.

00:33:19.050 --> 00:33:20.900
Course steady.

00:33:21.160 --> 00:33:22.820
All engines thrusting on schedule.

00:33:22.960 --> 00:33:23.760
Guidance A-OK.

00:33:24.230 --> 00:33:26.770
Your shoulders are tense and you're gripping the wheel too tightly.

00:33:26.930 --> 00:33:28.690
Relax and let the computer take over.

00:33:28.690 --> 00:33:29.510
Yes, sir.

00:33:30.060 --> 00:33:31.600
The bridge calling. Come in, Amuro.

00:33:32.310 --> 00:33:36.980
Don't let Gundam drift too far away from White Base. Stay ten kilometers ahead of the stern.

00:33:37.650 --> 00:33:41.820
We need to confirm that every section is sealed airtight. Can you manage that, John?

00:33:41.840 --> 00:33:42.480
Already did.

00:33:42.620 --> 00:33:47.360
Operator, the ship is being crewed by a lot of civilian amateurs. I want them caught up to speed as quickly as possible.

00:33:47.480 --> 00:33:49.740
It appears the civilians are doing surprisingly well, sir.

00:33:49.880 --> 00:33:50.160
Really?

00:33:50.480 --> 00:33:52.820
We run a daily inventory check of our supplies.

00:33:52.900 --> 00:33:54.520
I know. Internal data sequence.

00:33:54.600 --> 00:33:56.000
You catch on real quick, don't you?

00:33:56.120 --> 00:33:58.960
Our old battle station's manned and prepared for an enemy attack.

00:34:01.280 --> 00:34:03.020
They're as ready as they're ever going to be, sir.

00:34:05.450 --> 00:34:11.280
Begin the Minofsky broadcast.

00:34:11.460 --> 00:34:12.520
Begin ionization.

00:34:12.840 --> 00:34:13.760
Computer, take over.

00:34:17.020 --> 00:34:21.330
Warfighter, and I'm awaiting your command.

00:34:21.510 --> 00:34:22.690
Do you know how to fly that thing?

00:34:22.990 --> 00:34:23.870
I'm almost a pilot.

00:34:24.010 --> 00:34:25.050
I'm a qualified trainee.

00:34:25.640 --> 00:34:26.440
Better than nothing.

00:34:26.900 --> 00:34:29.640
How much experience do you have in terms of flying time?

00:34:30.030 --> 00:34:32.250
- I've logged two simulated flights.

00:34:32.250 --> 00:34:35.720
- Great, he's got almost as much experience as armor.

00:34:35.720 --> 00:34:38.580
- Incoming missiles, a pair of Annihilator-class nuke hits

00:34:38.580 --> 00:34:41.060
12 degrees to starboard, closing at Mach 3.

00:34:41.060 --> 00:34:41.900
- Hard about?

00:34:41.900 --> 00:34:43.210
- Maneuvering now.

00:34:43.210 --> 00:34:44.050
- Too late, Mira.

00:34:44.050 --> 00:34:44.810
- What?

00:34:44.810 --> 00:34:45.650
- I'd better try to get him.

00:34:45.650 --> 00:34:46.490
- Do it.

00:34:46.490 --> 00:34:48.050
- I'll be right with you.

00:34:48.050 --> 00:34:49.520
- He's a pie.

00:34:54.500 --> 00:34:58.250
Oh, come on.

00:34:58.250 --> 00:35:00.000
- Two more bogeys on same trajectory,

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:00.800
It's same coordinates

00:35:00.800 --> 00:35:01.480
Are them all missiles?

00:35:01.920 --> 00:35:03.340
They look more like mobile suits

00:35:03.340 --> 00:35:03.960
What speed?

00:35:04.240 --> 00:35:07.160
It's at least three times faster than any Zack who I've ever heard of, sir

00:35:07.160 --> 00:35:08.540
This has got to be something else

00:35:08.540 --> 00:35:10.460
There is one with that kind of speed

00:35:10.460 --> 00:35:12.200
Shaw, the red comet

00:35:12.200 --> 00:35:15.090
I was afraid he was going to find us eventually

00:35:15.090 --> 00:35:17.560
I couldn't hear everything you said

00:35:17.560 --> 00:35:19.490
Shaw, the red comet

00:35:19.490 --> 00:35:19.910
Shaw!

00:35:20.230 --> 00:35:23.000
He's the most feared Zeon of them all

00:35:23.000 --> 00:35:28.100
In just 15 minutes, he single-handedly took out five of our ships at the Battle of Rue

00:35:28.100 --> 00:35:30.000
Ah, quick, canon

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:41.780
the brand new mobile suit those fetties have designed looks good now it's going to get its

00:35:41.780 --> 00:35:49.140
first real test somehow shooting a zaku doesn't bother me as much as shooting people it isn't the

00:35:49.140 --> 00:35:57.430
same come back in amaro he's too much for you maybe not your dog meat huh

00:36:02.240 --> 00:36:12.340
Bye-bye what he took a direct hit, and he's still able to function this is it life or death and I have to pull myself together

00:36:23.560 --> 00:36:30.000
Slender hurry up and get behind him so we can attack them together, but sir I

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:33.340
I've never seen anything like it! I don't know if you and I can outmaneuver it!

00:36:33.340 --> 00:36:36.240
We all gotta die eventually, what are you so nervous about anyway?

00:36:36.240 --> 00:36:40.750
My energy is running low!

00:36:40.750 --> 00:36:43.760
You didn't have to tell me that, I was already aware of it!

00:36:43.760 --> 00:36:44.830
Whoa!

00:36:46.800 --> 00:36:54.280
Whoops!

00:36:54.280 --> 00:36:56.950
There's one behind you! Pull off!

00:37:00.160 --> 00:37:19.920
do that completely disintegrated him with one missile that thing must be

00:37:19.920 --> 00:37:23.440
equipped with a phaser cannon energized by neutron charges they've overtaken us

00:37:23.440 --> 00:37:29.800
in technological superiority man oh man unbelievable

00:37:30.540 --> 00:37:32.540
We're going to need a new battle plan.

00:37:32.690 --> 00:37:34.640
Then I shall return!

00:37:36.630 --> 00:37:41.890
Well, there went the last of my Phaser Neutrons.

00:37:42.910 --> 00:37:46.290
Damn, I have to let them get away.

00:38:02.010 --> 00:38:04.450
Corefighter secured. Gundam, approach for pickup.

00:38:05.440 --> 00:38:06.900
Gundam is locked on approach, sir.

00:38:07.280 --> 00:38:10.680
Inform Amuro and Rio I want them both to report to the bridge immediately.

00:38:11.080 --> 00:38:11.660
Yes, sir.

00:38:11.780 --> 00:38:13.600
Set white base on course for Luna 2.

00:38:13.760 --> 00:38:18.120
Inform the crew they may stand down for a rest break, but they must remain at battle posts and alert.

00:38:18.750 --> 00:38:20.200
The heroes are here, sir.

00:38:20.880 --> 00:38:23.220
So, what's that Zeon ship up to now?

00:38:23.440 --> 00:38:30.000
They're becalmed, hovering just outside of our firing range, but you can bet your O2 when we move out, Char's going to be right on our tail again.

00:38:32.170 --> 00:38:33.880
"That Gundam's impressive!"

00:38:33.880 --> 00:38:38.840
"Uh-huh. Needs a soldier to fly it all."

00:38:38.840 --> 00:38:48.280
"Right. Listen. In combat, the slightest hesitation can be fatal. You can't be indecisive when so many lives depend on you."

00:38:48.280 --> 00:38:51.180
"Uh-huh. Got it."

00:38:51.180 --> 00:38:58.490
"In war, it's kill or be killed. When you hesitate to fire at an enemy, be sure he'll take advantage of it. A Zeon won't give you a second chance."

00:38:58.490 --> 00:38:59.640
"Yeah, yeah."

00:39:00.220 --> 00:39:05.690
won it's a tough job that calls for a man if you can't handle it just tell me

00:39:05.690 --> 00:39:09.290
so right now you may think you're the right man for the job but you haven't

00:39:09.290 --> 00:39:14.540
convinced me he risked his life for us huh you don't have another pilot I'm it

00:39:14.540 --> 00:39:20.130
remember if you don't like the way I fly see if you can do better hold it I've

00:39:20.130 --> 00:39:24.610
already made my decision so go back to the Gundam and help the maintenance crew

00:39:24.610 --> 00:39:30.000
you pick whatever men you need I'm putting you in command of Gundam Amaro don't

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:34.760
ever make me regret my decision. If you do, I'll make sure you regret it even more.

00:39:41.420 --> 00:39:45.880
Luna 2, a wandering asteroid captured and brought here to serve as a weigh station and

00:39:45.880 --> 00:39:51.100
supply warehouse for colonial construction crews. It now serves as the frontline headquarters

00:39:51.100 --> 00:39:52.640
base of the federal forces.

00:40:01.340 --> 00:40:04.160
Canned foodians, how many people live here?

00:40:04.160 --> 00:40:06.110
We have seven here.

00:40:06.110 --> 00:40:09.270
Excuse me, but I requested some milk for my baby. Did they send it?

00:40:09.270 --> 00:40:10.800
Here it is!

00:40:10.800 --> 00:40:12.700
When are we scheduled to lock at Luna 2?

00:40:12.700 --> 00:40:14.200
In about an hour, I believe, sir.

00:40:14.200 --> 00:40:16.500
What time will the food rations be delivered this morning?

00:40:16.500 --> 00:40:17.900
They're on their way right now, ma'am.

00:40:17.900 --> 00:40:20.400
Sir!

00:40:20.400 --> 00:40:26.100
Where did you live before you moved out to Side 7?

00:40:26.100 --> 00:40:27.930
Do you have a reason for asking that?

00:40:27.930 --> 00:40:29.030
Just curious.

00:40:30.090 --> 00:40:31.000
Earth, sir.

00:40:31.000 --> 00:40:32.950
This is a first for me.

00:40:32.950 --> 00:40:33.390
Huh?

00:40:33.390 --> 00:40:35.010
My first time in space, I mean.

00:40:35.010 --> 00:40:37.270
This is coming very close to fraternizing.

00:40:37.270 --> 00:40:39.120
You mean we can't be friendly?

00:40:39.120 --> 00:40:42.720
Well, you haven't been all that friendly with any of the others.

00:40:42.720 --> 00:40:47.560
Wanna take a break? I can hold us on course, I think.

00:40:47.560 --> 00:40:50.160
Could you? I'll be back long before it's time to dock.

00:40:50.160 --> 00:40:51.670
Thank you, Sayla.

00:40:51.670 --> 00:40:53.320
Still with us.

00:40:53.320 --> 00:40:56.990
I'm sure that Xeon won't bother us while we're at Luna 2.

00:40:56.990 --> 00:40:58.080
Why not?

00:40:58.080 --> 00:40:59.760
They have bigger guns, sir.

00:41:05.150 --> 00:41:15.720
I knew it. You never stopped working, Amaro. If you don't get something to eat, you could die of starvation. You've already gone deaf, it would seem.

00:41:15.720 --> 00:41:19.720
I brought you a change of clothes, too. You don't want to start smelling funny.

00:41:19.720 --> 00:41:21.810
Hey, thanks a million, Frau.

00:41:21.810 --> 00:41:24.810
Thought you'd be furious at Noah Bright for making you do this dirty work.

00:41:24.810 --> 00:41:30.000
I'm not doing it because of him. I'm just doing it because I want to keep breathing.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:40.500
- Really? Is that your reason? - Yes.

00:41:40.500 --> 00:41:44.460
That old bucket of bolts should have been turned into scrap metal 25 years ago.

00:41:44.460 --> 00:41:45.860
- Give me a video link. - Sir.

00:41:45.860 --> 00:41:48.100
- I want the supply officer. - Sir.

00:41:48.100 --> 00:41:52.140
We got your frantic request for supplies. What are you doing? Shooting ducks with your missiles?

00:41:52.140 --> 00:41:54.560
We had our first encounter with the Fedi's new mobile suit.

00:41:54.560 --> 00:41:58.650
Just as I thought. That's why the whole sector is filling up with Manofsky particles.

00:41:58.650 --> 00:42:00.000
Hey, guess we're gonna have to hurry.

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:02.640
Open supply hatches and secure conveyor belts immediately.

00:42:13.150 --> 00:42:15.320
Madagascar, our beacon has a lock on you.

00:42:15.860 --> 00:42:17.500
Docking speed max minus two.

00:42:17.960 --> 00:42:19.460
You're in the pipe and looking good.

00:42:20.080 --> 00:42:21.460
Docking crew to your duty force.

00:42:21.560 --> 00:42:23.520
Madagascar entering port for R&R.

00:42:23.660 --> 00:42:26.720
Wreck services, stand by to receive stampeding troops.

00:42:27.160 --> 00:42:30.000
This is Recreation Service's virtual party program is...

00:42:30.060 --> 00:42:34.060
Up and running, they'll wake up tomorrow thinking they've had the time of their lives.

00:42:34.060 --> 00:42:35.990
Ammo loaders, report to Pier 2.

00:42:35.990 --> 00:42:41.120
Viping aboard Captain McGrew of White Base.

00:42:41.120 --> 00:42:47.890
Commander Joaquin, welcome to Luna 2, sir.

00:42:47.890 --> 00:42:51.570
We need repairs and we have orphaned children who need nurturing.

00:42:51.570 --> 00:42:52.530
Yes, sir.

00:42:52.530 --> 00:42:54.400
We can get your ship to Jabrow immediately.

00:42:54.400 --> 00:42:57.150
Everybody can stay on board.

00:42:57.150 --> 00:42:58.150
Take him right to sickbay.

00:42:58.150 --> 00:42:59.220
Sir.

00:43:05.080 --> 00:43:09.240
Excuse me, Commander Bokane. We need some experienced engineers to supervise our crew.

00:43:09.480 --> 00:43:13.700
We can't make it to Jabra, otherwise we'd have a bunch of civilian amateurs running our ship.

00:43:13.920 --> 00:43:16.120
The lives of all these refugees are at stake, sir.

00:43:16.660 --> 00:43:20.220
Hmm. Well, they may be rank amateurs, but they've done very well.

00:43:21.200 --> 00:43:21.460
Huh?

00:43:21.850 --> 00:43:23.000
But, sir...

00:43:23.000 --> 00:43:23.280
Hmm?

00:43:23.620 --> 00:43:27.110
Well, it's good to know he has so much concern about our welfare.

00:43:27.510 --> 00:43:30.000
I'm sorry, people, but my orders came directly from headquartered.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:34.080
quarters at Jabrow. They want White Base to leave immediately. I don't want to go to Jabrow.

00:43:34.320 --> 00:43:39.120
I came from Earth and I don't want to go back. I like Side 7. Yeah, why can't we go back to

00:43:39.120 --> 00:43:45.760
Side 7? Listen up. I have to obey my orders. White Base will leave for Jabrow at once. Sorry.

00:43:54.580 --> 00:43:58.730
Sir, do you think they have any chance of making it? The generals have no idea what

00:43:58.730 --> 00:44:00.000
it's like out here on the front.

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:03.010
Unfortunately, all I can do for those poor people is wish them luck.

00:44:03.010 --> 00:44:08.230
It's a real shame.

00:44:08.230 --> 00:44:10.830
No, I don't think they'll make it.

00:44:10.830 --> 00:44:15.010
The single cruiser escort that headquarters gave them is a joke.

00:44:15.010 --> 00:44:17.610
These are very troubled times we live in.

00:44:17.610 --> 00:44:20.010
War brings out the worst in everyone.

00:44:20.010 --> 00:44:23.030
I just hope White Base doesn't get captured, Robinson.

00:44:23.030 --> 00:44:25.960
The Federation's only hope for victory is Gundam.

00:44:42.220 --> 00:44:47.820
look for spare parts for a version 26 computer try the core fighter salvage pit so Gundam's

00:44:47.820 --> 00:44:53.860
cockpit is actually converted core fighter Gundam gun tank and gun cannon all use cores

00:44:53.860 --> 00:44:57.560
the suits built around them good good hold it

00:45:00.440 --> 00:45:03.010
You think they'll let you fly against a real enemy, Hayato?

00:45:03.010 --> 00:45:07.670
Well, now, that Xeon ship is right behind us. Why don't you bring it down?

00:45:07.670 --> 00:45:09.660
- Go away, little boy. - Yeah, right.

00:45:09.660 --> 00:45:13.280
You, Kai! Have you completed the maintenance on the gun cannon yet?

00:45:13.280 --> 00:45:14.380
Yes, ma'am.

00:45:14.380 --> 00:45:17.600
Well, now, I want you to go on standby at level 15. Now!

00:45:17.600 --> 00:45:18.950
Yes, sir.

00:45:18.950 --> 00:45:21.190
25 minutes to atmospheric entry.

00:45:21.190 --> 00:45:22.770
Can you handle this all right, may I?

00:45:22.770 --> 00:45:24.870
I did get to fly one entry when I was a student,

00:45:24.870 --> 00:45:27.080
and had the ground control commnet seeing to it

00:45:27.080 --> 00:45:30.000
that I didn't commit any gigantically dangerous errors.

00:45:30.060 --> 00:45:32.900
Don't worry. Just follow the escort and do whatever they say.

00:45:33.160 --> 00:45:36.890
Got it. What I'm really worried about is Shaw. He's not going to just sit there and let us get away.

00:45:36.890 --> 00:45:40.030
You just concentrate on the re-entry and let me worry about the fighting.

00:45:40.110 --> 00:45:40.750
Understood, sir.

00:45:41.060 --> 00:45:41.620
You're there, kid?

00:45:41.800 --> 00:45:42.800
Yes, Lieutenant Reed?

00:45:43.390 --> 00:45:48.320
I'm in our re-entry capsule now. Just wanted to check in with you guys to make sure you're ready for the big adventure.

00:45:48.440 --> 00:45:50.880
We'll be increasing airspeed. Be sure you don't fall behind.

00:45:51.200 --> 00:45:53.080
Roger. We'll stay right behind you, sir.

00:45:53.660 --> 00:45:59.310
Okay, let's do it, Mirai. Cut in the auto-nav system and notify everybody to buckle up and prepare for re-entry.

00:45:59.570 --> 00:46:00.000
Aye, aye.

00:46:00.860 --> 00:46:04.760
With three new Zakus we have superior numbers as well as superior power.

00:46:04.760 --> 00:46:07.200
We also have the element of timing in our favor.

00:46:07.200 --> 00:46:11.310
The plan is to launch our attack while the FETI's complete attention is focused on re-entry.

00:46:11.310 --> 00:46:13.000
That's 20 minutes from now.

00:46:13.000 --> 00:46:16.200
Be extremely careful to stay outside the range of the Earth's gravity,

00:46:16.200 --> 00:46:19.330
because if it should pull you in, your Zaku will be incinerated.

00:46:19.330 --> 00:46:22.060
Your only target will be their Solomus re-entry capsule,

00:46:22.060 --> 00:46:24.360
and if they launch their mobile suit, which is very likely,

00:46:24.360 --> 00:46:26.820
leave that to me and don't let it distract you.

00:46:26.820 --> 00:46:30.000
Without the Solomus to guide them, there's no way white

00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:33.780
base can possibly make it through re-entry alive. To victory!

00:46:33.780 --> 00:46:39.920
We'll be entering Earth's atmosphere in 15 minutes. All crews stand by as alert level

00:46:39.920 --> 00:46:40.770
3.

00:46:40.770 --> 00:46:42.990
Would you look at this suit they gave me?

00:46:42.990 --> 00:46:48.190
They must have some kids' outfits. Somebody made a dumb mistake.

00:46:48.190 --> 00:46:51.010
It has a double buckle, Amro. You want that thing airtight?

00:46:51.010 --> 00:46:55.120
Forget a kid's outfit. Mine fits fine.

00:46:55.120 --> 00:46:58.720
Boy, what happened to me? How did I get into this war?

00:46:58.720 --> 00:47:00.000
What's that?

00:47:00.030 --> 00:47:08.390
come on make sure your missiles are armed and ready affirmative sir you think shall follow us

00:47:08.390 --> 00:47:16.180
not if he's smart the solomus is now launched so buckle up white base will be following it on an

