equal speed program attention everyone on board we will enter earth's atmosphere in approximately

00:47:29.060 --> 00:47:30.000
three minutes

00:47:30.120 --> 00:47:30.520
Quiet!

00:47:31.030 --> 00:47:35.090
Remain seated, but don't be alarmed when we experience heavy vibration.

00:47:35.510 --> 00:47:36.530
It's perfectly normal.

00:47:36.730 --> 00:47:41.510
Combat and maintenance personnel remain at your stations in case we have to launch the Gundam.

00:47:41.900 --> 00:47:43.780
Remain alert and prepared for anything.

00:47:44.100 --> 00:47:44.800
Prepare to scramble.

00:47:45.280 --> 00:47:46.040
Bandits sighted.

00:47:46.140 --> 00:47:47.680
Interception in 34 seconds.

00:47:48.120 --> 00:47:49.980
Three common class zakus and one customized.

00:47:53.280 --> 00:48:00.000
Gundam, we need you to slow down those zakus until white base has entered atmosphere.

00:48:00.640 --> 00:48:06.340
Amuro, after you launch, you'll only have four minutes to return to White Base before you encounter atmospheric friction.

00:48:06.340 --> 00:48:07.940
Four minutes?

00:48:07.940 --> 00:48:10.720
Otherwise, the friction will melt and evaporate the Gundam.

00:48:10.720 --> 00:48:13.220
Yeah, yeah, I know. You don't have to describe it to me.

00:48:13.220 --> 00:48:17.600
Keep monitoring your altitude constantly so you don't get captured by Earth's gravity pool.

00:48:17.600 --> 00:48:20.240
Sure. What's wrong? I don't have enough to do?

00:48:20.240 --> 00:48:24.460
Ryu and Kai will be flying cover. All of us have complete confidence in the three of you.

00:48:24.460 --> 00:48:26.930
Thanks a million. I only wish I shared that confidence.

00:48:26.930 --> 00:48:28.740
I know you'll bring us through this, Amuro.

00:48:28.740 --> 00:48:30.000
You sound just like a high school.

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:30.500
Gold Cheerleader

00:48:30.500 --> 00:48:31.100
Stand by to launch

00:48:31.100 --> 00:48:33.780
It's time

00:48:33.780 --> 00:48:34.520
Gundam away

00:48:34.520 --> 00:48:35.240
Roger

00:48:35.240 --> 00:48:43.380
We're all depending on you Amaro

00:48:43.380 --> 00:48:44.620
Don't let them down

00:48:44.620 --> 00:48:48.820
The three of you split up

00:48:48.820 --> 00:48:50.060
And attack the supporting cover

00:48:50.060 --> 00:48:51.560
Doran you fly back up for them

00:48:51.560 --> 00:48:53.080
While I challenge that new mobile suit

00:48:53.080 --> 00:48:53.980
To a one on one

00:48:53.980 --> 00:48:54.780
I copy sir

00:48:54.780 --> 00:48:55.680
Go get him

00:48:55.680 --> 00:48:57.060
Reentry capsule is now ready

00:48:57.060 --> 00:48:58.420
We will launch on your order sir

00:48:58.420 --> 00:48:59.060
Go ahead

00:48:59.060 --> 00:48:59.860
Launch it

00:49:03.550 --> 00:49:05.830
Sir! Cover missiles on their way!

00:49:05.830 --> 00:49:26.780
I tracked you!

00:49:26.780 --> 00:49:28.940
Zakus are going after the Solomus Capsule!

00:49:28.940 --> 00:49:29.830
The Capsule?

00:49:32.560 --> 00:49:33.720
I'll get Sha later.

00:49:35.450 --> 00:49:37.020
But I'm lined up point blank.

00:49:39.270 --> 00:49:43.930
It lost focus.

00:49:47.770 --> 00:49:49.070
Sight slipped out of calibration.

00:49:49.710 --> 00:49:50.210
Oh boy.

00:49:52.030 --> 00:49:54.740
Sir, that means projected by some kind of energy shield.

00:49:56.680 --> 00:49:58.260
Help! The foe's apart!

00:49:58.260 --> 00:49:59.160
Oh!

00:50:03.580 --> 00:50:04.470
What's going on?

00:50:04.470 --> 00:50:06.760
Maybe the Vulcan cannon barrel is misaligned.

00:50:06.760 --> 00:50:07.770
Huh?

00:50:07.770 --> 00:50:11.010
We've been hit bad, sir.

00:50:11.010 --> 00:50:12.010
Losing pressure!

00:50:12.010 --> 00:50:13.510
You have to abort the guided re-entry.

00:50:13.510 --> 00:50:15.010
Looks like you're on your own, kid.

00:50:15.010 --> 00:50:16.290
We bought the farm this time.

00:50:16.290 --> 00:50:17.790
We won't abandon you.

00:50:17.790 --> 00:50:19.010
Prepare to board White Base.

00:50:19.010 --> 00:50:20.090
Thanks.

00:50:20.090 --> 00:50:23.890
Sailor, tell Amuro to lure those Akus away from Solomus.

00:50:23.890 --> 00:50:25.170
Amuro is under attack by Shaw.

00:50:25.170 --> 00:50:28.070
He'll be lucky if he can save his own life.

00:50:32.170 --> 00:50:33.650
I'm in real trouble now!

00:50:33.650 --> 00:50:37.550
No question about it, that thing is one magnificent weapon.

00:50:37.550 --> 00:50:39.550
But any mobile suit is only as good as its pilot.

00:50:41.240 --> 00:50:42.240
This is gonna be fun!

00:50:45.330 --> 00:50:50.250
Got him now!

00:50:50.250 --> 00:50:51.250
It's time for sure!

00:50:51.250 --> 00:50:54.630
I don't believe it!

00:50:54.630 --> 00:50:56.120
Is everything out of alignment?

00:50:56.120 --> 00:50:58.430
He's behind me now!

00:50:58.430 --> 00:50:59.860
Now!

00:51:04.600 --> 00:51:05.800
*laughs*

00:51:05.800 --> 00:51:08.750
Stand by for pickup, Solomus. Deploying laser locks.

00:51:08.750 --> 00:51:11.770
Hurry, those Zakus are coming right up behind us.

00:51:11.770 --> 00:51:13.770
No problem, we've got you now.

00:51:14.660 --> 00:51:20.350
I'll never let you get in this way.

00:51:20.350 --> 00:51:23.140
You have to close in on him.

00:51:23.140 --> 00:51:26.050
No! We haven't been able to penetrate the heavy artillery fire!

00:51:26.050 --> 00:51:29.380
Take advantage of their weaknesses. Try attacking from below.

00:51:31.280 --> 00:51:32.380
Are they going to hit starboard?

00:51:32.520 --> 00:51:34.200
We need more firepower, starboard. Quickly!

00:51:34.670 --> 00:51:37.920
I am now releasing emergency bulkhead sealants in all affected areas.

00:51:38.060 --> 00:51:40.220
Why won't you let us go out and watch the fighting, frown?

00:51:40.240 --> 00:51:41.360
It's too dangerous, Kika.

00:51:41.520 --> 00:51:42.340
I'm not scared.

00:51:42.440 --> 00:51:43.340
Well, you should be.

00:51:43.540 --> 00:51:44.560
I want to fight.

00:51:44.800 --> 00:51:47.060
I don't even know where the machine gun turrets are.

00:51:47.380 --> 00:51:50.880
Starboard 35 aims forward. It's up ahead on your left. You can't miss it.

00:51:50.880 --> 00:51:51.920
Ahead on my left.

00:52:00.030 --> 00:52:03.590
We've got Zakos attacking from below. Amuro, is there any way to bring Gundam in?

00:52:03.590 --> 00:52:04.490
How bad is it, Bright?

00:52:04.490 --> 00:52:06.630
Well, it could be a whole lot better.

00:52:06.630 --> 00:52:07.990
Nice!

00:52:07.990 --> 00:52:17.330
Huh? Huh?

00:52:17.330 --> 00:52:20.220
Sir?

00:52:20.220 --> 00:52:21.570
Petra Jets on!

00:52:30.160 --> 00:52:31.320
That should have done it.

00:52:32.290 --> 00:52:33.840
It's much tougher than I thought.

00:52:33.880 --> 00:52:35.440
Gundam, come back to base immediately.

00:52:36.540 --> 00:52:38.620
Amuro, atmospheric re-entry is underway.

00:52:38.820 --> 00:52:39.840
Return to white base.

00:52:40.080 --> 00:52:41.800
Battle all hatches and retract your guns.

00:52:41.980 --> 00:52:42.940
Secure for re-entry.

00:52:44.540 --> 00:52:47.600
Amuro, landing bay 45 is standing by to receive you.

00:52:47.780 --> 00:52:48.560
Come in immediately.

00:52:48.820 --> 00:52:49.620
I'm on my way.

00:52:51.650 --> 00:52:54.230
Commander Shah, you must return to the re-entry capsule.

00:52:54.680 --> 00:52:58.550
Crown, if you don't want your Zaku to melt, disengage and return to the capsule immediately.

00:52:58.890 --> 00:53:00.000
The Feti won't make it anyway.

00:53:01.760 --> 00:53:05.520
Amuro is still dueling with that Zaku, and they're both beginning to burn! He has to

00:53:05.520 --> 00:53:06.880
come in right now, sir!

00:53:06.880 --> 00:53:09.020
Amuro, I'm ordering you to return now!

00:53:09.020 --> 00:53:14.280
Ensign Bright, if we show up at Jabro without the Gundam, we're going to be in serious trouble,

00:53:14.280 --> 00:53:16.800
so tell that youngster to quit fooling around!

00:53:16.800 --> 00:53:18.400
What's the matter with that kid, anyway?

00:53:18.400 --> 00:53:21.570
I'm the one who ordered it launched.

00:53:21.570 --> 00:53:25.130
If Amuro hadn't been out there risking his life, White Base would have been destroyed

00:53:25.130 --> 00:53:26.140
by the enemy!

00:53:26.140 --> 00:53:30.000
Lieutenant Reed, we've begun atmospheric re-entry, so find a seat someplace and fill it. We don't

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:31.760
I don't want to have any unnecessary injuries.

00:53:31.760 --> 00:53:33.940
I'll see two at your court-martial for this, mister.

00:53:33.940 --> 00:53:43.610
Where's Amuro? Why isn't he back from his mission yet? When? Oh!

00:53:43.610 --> 00:53:48.630
Oh no! I didn't pull out quick enough and now I've been caught up in gravity!

00:53:48.630 --> 00:53:50.220
Doran, what happened to Crown?

00:53:50.220 --> 00:53:53.690
We'll just have to forget about him. It's too late to recover him, Commander.

00:53:53.690 --> 00:53:57.250
Commander Shaw, I can't slow down! Stockwood doesn't respond!

00:53:57.250 --> 00:54:00.000
I think I've been caught by gravity and I don't know what to do!

00:54:00.640 --> 00:54:02.240
before you gotta help me!

00:54:02.240 --> 00:54:04.720
Crown, we're already too deep in the atmosphere.

00:54:04.720 --> 00:54:06.670
There isn't time to recover you.

00:54:06.670 --> 00:54:08.710
Nothing can save you now.

00:54:08.710 --> 00:54:10.180
I'm sorry, Crown.

00:54:10.180 --> 00:54:22.700
Your name will go down in history.

00:54:22.700 --> 00:54:25.000
There it is, gravitational reentry system.

00:54:25.000 --> 00:54:26.510
Now I just hope I have enough time

00:54:26.510 --> 00:54:28.610
to find this thing and figure out how it operates.

00:54:28.610 --> 00:54:30.000
Here goes nothing.

00:54:37.610 --> 00:54:41.040
I'm no longer in communication with Gundam due to re-entry blackout.

00:54:41.040 --> 00:54:43.060
Amoro! Amoro!

00:54:43.060 --> 00:54:44.190
Coming, Gundam!

00:54:44.190 --> 00:54:46.190
What's going on, Sailor? What's happening? What's wrong?

00:54:46.190 --> 00:54:48.170
Don't worry, this is normal during re-entry.

00:54:48.170 --> 00:54:51.170
The friction heat hasn't even affected it. I wonder what their secret is.

00:54:51.170 --> 00:54:54.170
It would appear they've perfected a mobile suit cooling system, sir.

00:54:54.170 --> 00:54:57.170
It must utilize liquid oxygen, like white base.

00:54:57.170 --> 00:55:00.000
Our rate of descent is steady. 27?

00:55:00.220 --> 00:55:10.290
26, 25, 24, 23, 22, 21, 20, 19, 18.

00:55:11.980 --> 00:55:15.640
Hang in there. We can do it.

00:55:16.580 --> 00:55:19.640
As soon as we establish communication with Earth, contact Captain Garma.

00:55:19.900 --> 00:55:22.850
You made them change their re-entry angle. Is that correct?

00:55:22.850 --> 00:55:26.810
Yes. They don't realize it, but they'll be landing in territory that we control.

00:55:27.300 --> 00:55:29.510
Absolutely brilliant, sir. I congratulate you.

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:34.310
You must say that your very enviable reputation is most highly deserved, Commander Shah.

00:55:34.310 --> 00:55:38.320
The war game is unforgiving. You must always be one step ahead of your enemy.

00:55:38.320 --> 00:55:44.470
I've contacted Captain Garma, Commander.

00:55:44.470 --> 00:55:48.230
I'm afraid that I have nothing but unhappy news to report to you, Captain.

00:55:48.230 --> 00:55:50.070
Have you heard about the V Project?

00:55:50.070 --> 00:55:52.390
You mean the Fetty super secret weapon?

00:55:52.390 --> 00:55:55.800
That's right. And it isn't just a rumor, sir. I've encountered it.

00:55:55.800 --> 00:55:58.390
That monster from hell brought down six of my Zakus.

00:55:58.390 --> 00:55:59.320
Incredible.

00:56:00.600 --> 00:56:04.300
landing here so you could have the honor of destroying it personally, Captain.

00:56:04.300 --> 00:56:05.300
Thank you.

00:56:05.300 --> 00:56:08.050
I accept your gracious offer.

00:56:08.050 --> 00:56:12.350
I'll be coming out of re-entry right behind them, and I'll be reporting their exact location.

00:56:12.350 --> 00:56:14.150
You can take them completely by surprise.

00:56:14.150 --> 00:56:17.670
I'll pounce on them with my Gau assault carriers before they even have a chance to recover

00:56:17.670 --> 00:56:18.670
from re-entry.

00:56:18.670 --> 00:56:28.140
Adjutant, call a scramble immediately.

00:56:28.140 --> 00:56:29.570
Video is coming back, sir!

00:56:30.830 --> 00:56:32.820
Look, sir, the Gundam made it!

00:56:32.820 --> 00:56:35.150
Komuro!

00:56:35.150 --> 00:56:36.890
In my heart, I never had a doubt.

00:56:36.890 --> 00:56:38.070
He made it!

00:56:38.070 --> 00:56:56.620
That's Earth, youngster, where all of us people originated.

00:56:56.620 --> 00:56:59.320
It looks just like the pictures you showed me, Grandpa!

00:57:00.860 --> 00:57:02.690
It must be the ocean, right?

00:57:02.690 --> 00:57:04.110
Yes, that's right.

00:57:04.110 --> 00:57:07.270
Now that I think of it, you've never seen an ocean before, have you?

00:57:07.270 --> 00:57:08.670
Remember what this looks like.

00:57:08.670 --> 00:57:12.100
There's not another place in the whole universe as beautiful as Earth.

00:57:12.100 --> 00:57:12.930
Bar none.

00:57:30.480 --> 00:57:33.130
- Good work, Amuro.

00:57:33.130 --> 00:57:40.220
- Hm.

00:57:40.220 --> 00:57:44.670
- What's wrong?

00:57:44.670 --> 00:57:45.510
- Huh?

00:57:50.680 --> 00:57:52.400
- Having a party to celebrate your victory

00:57:52.400 --> 00:57:53.760
and you're our special guest.

00:57:53.760 --> 00:57:55.930
- We brought champagne for our toast.

00:57:55.930 --> 00:57:58.500
- And look, hooray for Amuro, he's my hero.

00:57:58.500 --> 00:58:00.000
- Three cheers for Amuro, hippie.

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:00.720
Hip hooray!

00:58:01.570 --> 00:58:01.970
Thanks.

00:58:02.510 --> 00:58:04.010
Now go away and leave me alone.

00:58:04.370 --> 00:58:04.670
Alright?

00:58:05.130 --> 00:58:06.020
I need to rest.

00:58:08.480 --> 00:58:08.840
Boom!

00:58:31.660 --> 00:58:35.990
This was our projected touchdown point, and this is our current line of descent.

00:58:35.990 --> 00:58:39.010
We're gonna be coming down deep inside Zeon territory!

00:58:39.010 --> 00:58:42.590
Yes, I can see that. There's no way we can make it to Jabra now, is there?

00:58:42.590 --> 00:58:44.070
What were you thinking?

00:58:44.070 --> 00:58:46.140
You're wounded, sir. Let me take a look at that.

00:58:46.140 --> 00:58:48.800
Shah certainly pulled the wool over our eyes that time.

00:58:48.800 --> 00:58:50.420
We're right where he wants us.

00:58:50.420 --> 00:58:52.480
And he's given our position to everyone.

00:58:52.480 --> 00:58:55.320
White base must not be captured. We may have to scuttle it.

00:58:55.320 --> 00:58:56.280
Enemy planes!

00:58:56.280 --> 00:58:57.270
Already?

00:59:19.230 --> 00:59:21.490
new weapon isn't a rumor, eh?

00:59:21.490 --> 00:59:24.710
Commander Shaw was extremely impressed by the armaments and capabilities of the mobile

00:59:24.710 --> 00:59:25.560
suit.

00:59:25.560 --> 00:59:27.490
Moosai Capsule is here, sir.

00:59:27.490 --> 00:59:28.930
Beam the commander aboard.

00:59:28.930 --> 00:59:29.540
At once.

00:59:37.260 --> 00:59:43.040
If the anti-capsule is captured safely, notify Captain Garma that Commander Shah is on his way.

00:59:43.040 --> 00:59:50.120
Welcome aboard. I was surprised to hear you admit you'd been overwhelmed by one single enemy ship, Commander.

00:59:50.120 --> 00:59:55.220
Believe me, it gives me no pleasure to have to admit such a thing to the Division Commander of Earth Forces, Captain Garma.

00:59:55.220 --> 00:59:58.490
Call me Garma in memory of our happy days at the Academy Shah.

00:59:58.490 --> 01:00:00.000
We have a real problem, Garma.

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:04.000
Ah, yes. The new feti weapons sound like worthy opponents and I'll be eager to see them in action.

01:00:04.000 --> 01:00:08.430
Are you saying that's the only reason you came out here personally, to see them in action?

01:00:08.430 --> 01:00:12.660
No. I came to pick up a dear old friend of mine named Shaw. Remember?

01:00:12.660 --> 01:00:17.740
About the suit. Did they tell you that it was able to survive re-entry without suffering any damage?

01:00:17.740 --> 01:00:22.640
Yes. And did they tell you that the code name we've given to the white base project is Trojan Horse?

01:00:22.640 --> 01:00:27.940
Considering the historical context, I find that rather disturbingly fascinating, don't you?

01:00:27.940 --> 01:00:29.640
You look exhausted.

01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:31.860
Yes, they've been working me extremely hard.

01:00:32.310 --> 01:00:32.930
It's worth it.

01:00:33.570 --> 01:00:36.470
You'll probably win the Zeon Cross for defeating White Base Garma.

01:00:36.590 --> 01:00:37.150
Very likely.

01:00:37.530 --> 01:00:40.030
And I appreciate this great opportunity to prove my worth.

01:00:40.590 --> 01:00:44.190
It's even possible that it may help elevate my reputation in the eyes of my sister.

01:00:45.030 --> 01:00:45.510
Yes.

01:00:47.830 --> 01:00:49.010
The crew is watching.

01:00:49.490 --> 01:00:50.610
Stop laughing at me.

01:00:52.330 --> 01:00:55.480
Amuro, it's me, Fra Bo.

01:00:56.890 --> 01:00:57.880
Amuro?

01:00:58.350 --> 01:00:59.460
Amuro, come on!

01:01:03.960 --> 01:01:04.660
Is it a fever?

01:01:05.420 --> 01:01:06.970
No, Frau, it's nothing.

01:01:07.070 --> 01:01:07.770
What's the matter?

01:01:08.150 --> 01:01:09.050
Go away.

01:01:09.330 --> 01:01:11.590
They've placed you on permanent combat standby orders.

01:01:11.980 --> 01:01:13.720
I don't want to play with them anymore, Frau.

01:01:14.340 --> 01:01:16.840
Since leaving Side 7, I haven't had a wink of sleep.

01:01:17.720 --> 01:01:20.640
I close my eyes and try to relax, but my mind keeps racing.

01:01:21.740 --> 01:01:23.560
Let me ask Sailor to give you an examination.

01:01:24.400 --> 01:01:27.020
She's a third-year medical student. She might be able to help.

01:01:27.220 --> 01:01:28.290
Just go away.

01:01:29.000 --> 01:01:30.000
What is bothering you?

01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:34.170
you. You could tell me. I didn't ask for this war and I don't want to be a part of it anymore,

01:01:34.170 --> 01:01:38.730
Frau. None of us want war, but we're all involved in it whether we want it or not. We must protect

01:01:38.730 --> 01:01:43.030
the Federation from being overthrown by the rebel forces or we'll find ourselves doomed to slavery

01:01:43.030 --> 01:01:49.770
forever. Amuro, please, tell me what you're thinking. We're nothing more than sacrificial

01:01:49.770 --> 01:01:55.670
lambs. The federal forces are using us. I don't understand. They're just using us as

01:01:55.670 --> 01:02:00.000
decoys to keep the rebel forces occupied while they develop bigger and better weapons

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:05.480
in their labs we're expendable our lives mean absolutely nothing to them frow jabro headquarters

01:02:05.480 --> 01:02:12.090
has made contact lost go ahead jabro defense force m4 initialized decryption circuit alpha

01:02:12.090 --> 01:02:21.810
gain welcome jabro and out sorry sir they're joking we've been ordered to break through the

01:02:21.810 --> 01:02:26.200
enemy lines and escape to the sea but there's no suggestion as to how we're supposed to do it

01:02:26.200 --> 01:02:29.920
they aren't going to send us any assistance can we send them a reply through m4

01:02:30.190 --> 01:02:31.150
This must be a mistake!

01:02:31.150 --> 01:02:35.590
Sorry, sir. Even an encrypted message from inside enemy territory is expressly forbidden.

01:02:36.370 --> 01:02:38.950
What can those generals possibly be thinking about, Reed?

01:02:39.030 --> 01:02:41.090
I guess they just don't understand our situation.

01:02:41.550 --> 01:02:43.530
I suddenly have a bad feeling about this, Garma.

01:02:44.130 --> 01:02:45.710
I don't want you to go out there.

01:02:46.040 --> 01:02:49.480
If any person alive should be able to understand my motives, it ought to be you.

01:02:50.000 --> 01:02:52.500
You know how desperately I need to prove myself to my sister.

01:03:02.750 --> 01:03:04.510
Karma Squadron, prepare to follow your leader.

01:03:08.760 --> 01:03:13.540
You're dropping too low.

01:03:13.660 --> 01:03:14.840
Bring her up, bring her up.

01:03:15.680 --> 01:03:21.420
It's obvious your amateur Helms person has had no experience in low altitude flight.

01:03:21.540 --> 01:03:22.820
Take us up to a thousand feet.

01:03:23.130 --> 01:03:24.790
Their radar would pick us up in no time.

01:03:25.090 --> 01:03:29.060
I won't just sit here and allow White Base to be destroyed by crashing into a mountaintop.

01:03:29.330 --> 01:03:30.000
Don't blame me.

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:32.740
when the enemy spots us then.

01:03:32.740 --> 01:03:36.680
Ryu, are Kai and Hayato standing by?

01:03:36.680 --> 01:03:39.720
Yes sir, the forward turret of the gun tank is being manned by Hayato.

01:03:39.720 --> 01:03:40.440
Where's Kai?

01:03:40.440 --> 01:03:42.080
He's piloting the gun cannon.

01:03:42.080 --> 01:03:43.140
He'll be okay.

01:03:43.140 --> 01:03:44.020
Kai, are you ready?

01:03:44.020 --> 01:03:45.780
Define ready for me, Ryu.

01:03:45.780 --> 01:03:46.650
Carry on.

01:03:46.650 --> 01:03:48.900
We're gonna need all of the help we can get.

01:03:48.900 --> 01:03:51.700
If we didn't, I wouldn't be sending children out there.

01:03:52.380 --> 01:03:54.150
I won't fly against them.

01:03:54.150 --> 01:03:57.320
I'll take up a position on the ground under the cover of White Base.

01:03:57.320 --> 01:03:59.960
I'm not nearly as crazy as you might think.

01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:02.160
Going up against them in the air is committing suicide.

01:04:02.340 --> 01:04:03.740
You'll all get medals for this.

01:04:04.210 --> 01:04:05.290
Am I right, Captain Reed?

01:04:05.850 --> 01:04:07.410
They'll receive badges of valor.

01:04:08.180 --> 01:04:09.000
Good luck, men.

01:04:09.140 --> 01:04:09.970
Oh, Amuro.

01:04:10.610 --> 01:04:12.220
Go ahead, Fraubo, report.

01:04:12.400 --> 01:04:14.180
Amuro refuses to continue fighting.

01:04:14.440 --> 01:04:15.180
He's adamant.

01:04:15.200 --> 01:04:15.940
Huh? What did you say?

01:04:16.260 --> 01:04:16.980
Now what?

01:04:17.060 --> 01:04:19.060
Listen, Amuro, you will launch immediately.

01:04:19.200 --> 01:04:19.820
That's an order.

01:04:20.140 --> 01:04:22.020
If I should happen to survive and come back,

01:04:22.080 --> 01:04:23.540
do you guarantee I'll be able to sleep?

01:04:23.680 --> 01:04:24.660
What are you talking about?

01:04:24.940 --> 01:04:25.400
Amuro.

01:04:26.300 --> 01:04:27.870
I'm sorry, Fraubo.

01:04:27.870 --> 01:04:29.090
I can't take it anymore.

01:04:30.030 --> 01:04:36.110
if you hadn't fought before we'd be dead aren't we worth fighting for I can't

01:04:36.110 --> 01:04:54.930
frau I can't fight I'm coward coward coward nothing phases that thing heads

01:04:54.930 --> 01:04:58.600
up they're coming around behind us now it's a squadron of dots they're trying

01:04:58.600 --> 01:05:00.000
to cut off our escape room

01:05:05.950 --> 01:05:10.300
I'm Jack, a force now standing by for launch!

01:05:10.300 --> 01:05:11.300
Ready, Hayato!

01:05:11.300 --> 01:05:14.390
Roger, Ryu. I am ready.

01:05:14.390 --> 01:05:16.390
Attention! Gun tank, you're cleared for launch!

01:05:16.390 --> 01:05:18.210
Cover port site forward!

01:05:18.210 --> 01:05:22.210
Don't waste any more time! Launch!

01:05:35.720 --> 01:05:38.500
If that's all the firepower we can throw together, we're in trouble.

01:05:38.700 --> 01:05:39.920
Isn't Gundam coming out?

01:05:40.000 --> 01:05:41.700
Concentrate on your own assignment, Kai.

01:05:41.780 --> 01:05:44.320
When you need backup firepower, Gundam will be there.

01:05:44.580 --> 01:05:45.680
Hello, Sailor.

01:05:46.000 --> 01:05:48.170
I had a dream about you last night, sweetie.

01:05:48.310 --> 01:05:49.710
Altitude is 100 meters.

01:05:50.190 --> 01:05:51.470
Launch bay 12, attention.

01:05:52.030 --> 01:05:53.130
Standing by for exit.

01:05:53.590 --> 01:05:54.090
Open hatch.

01:05:56.600 --> 01:05:57.380
Attention, Ryu.

01:05:57.480 --> 01:05:58.480
You're clear for exit.

01:05:58.850 --> 01:05:59.940
Just stabilize your balance.

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:05.000
Alright, here we go, Hayato. Don't forget to release the safety on the cannon as soon as we get clear!

01:06:05.000 --> 01:06:08.820
You don't have to worry. I'm gonna show you all I'm as good as Amuro!

01:06:08.820 --> 01:06:17.930
What's that contraption? It looks like a tank!

01:06:17.930 --> 01:06:20.910
It's a defective design that they've gone and turned into a ground weapon.

01:06:20.910 --> 01:06:22.910
Why would the Fettis want to launch such an embarrassment?

01:06:22.910 --> 01:06:26.210
Who knows, maybe they were expecting us to attack with cavalry.

01:06:26.210 --> 01:06:29.090
Hayato! Bandits at 12 o'clock!

01:06:29.090 --> 01:06:29.670
Right!

01:06:38.860 --> 01:06:46.820
A real punch!

01:06:46.820 --> 01:06:47.820
Two more waves are coming in.

01:06:47.820 --> 01:06:48.820
We'll be counting on you, Kai.

01:06:48.820 --> 01:06:50.160
Good luck.

01:06:50.160 --> 01:06:51.160
Roger.

01:06:51.160 --> 01:06:51.920
I'm gonna do my best.

01:07:01.470 --> 01:07:03.400
Alright! I made it down!

01:07:03.400 --> 01:07:11.570
Huh! There's bad guys everywhere!

01:07:11.570 --> 01:07:13.990
*grunt*

01:07:31.120 --> 01:07:33.120
I pushed him back!

01:07:33.120 --> 01:07:37.970
I got him running!

01:07:37.970 --> 01:07:40.900
Attention Garmo Wing!

01:07:40.900 --> 01:07:42.900
Employing Modella Formation!

01:07:42.900 --> 01:07:44.900
White base has now launched a second mobile suit!

01:07:44.900 --> 01:07:46.880
Stay alert! This is Shaw.

01:07:46.880 --> 01:07:49.020
Did you say they've launched another mobile suit?

01:07:49.020 --> 01:07:50.910
Is it a white one? Negative.

01:07:50.910 --> 01:07:52.930
Both of these are standard ground assault models.

01:07:52.930 --> 01:07:55.940
They haven't launched the big guy for some reason.

01:07:55.940 --> 01:08:00.000
I won't win any medals fighting these puny rejects!

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:03.500
doesn't realize what serious danger he's in I'd better get down there and keep an

01:08:03.500 --> 01:08:12.280
eye on him I order you to launch Gundam get out there if it means so much to you

01:08:12.280 --> 01:08:15.760
why don't you fly the Gundam if I knew how to fly it I'd be out there in a

01:08:15.760 --> 01:08:19.350
minute and you know it what's wrong with you can beat me up and threaten to

01:08:19.350 --> 01:08:23.010
court-martial me but you can't make me go into combat against my will if you

01:08:23.010 --> 01:08:26.970
don't like that too bad wake up we're in a war Amaro and we

01:08:26.970 --> 01:08:30.000
don't have time for a philosophical debate I'm not being

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:35.640
philosophical actually i'm just flat out afraid oh yeah i'll give you something to be afraid of

01:08:35.640 --> 01:08:41.110
you settle everything with violence stop it sir why we don't have any witnesses he must be in

01:08:41.110 --> 01:08:46.850
shock and i've heard a slap can sometimes bring a traumatized victim out of it oh really better

01:08:46.850 --> 01:08:54.680
try again i'm still not convinced you may be an officer but i won't just stand here and take this

01:08:54.680 --> 01:09:00.000
oh was that a challenge i advise you think about that twice because i might take you up on it

01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:02.020
I won't go back into combat.

01:09:02.020 --> 01:09:05.100
You'll just have to train somebody else to fly Gundam for you.

01:09:05.100 --> 01:09:06.470
Oh, is that so?

01:09:06.470 --> 01:09:07.480
Listen here.

01:09:07.480 --> 01:09:09.360
I've never known you to be a whiner, Amuro.

01:09:09.360 --> 01:09:10.800
So get over it.

01:09:10.800 --> 01:09:13.100
I know it's difficult for you to do, but you must--

01:09:13.100 --> 01:09:14.100
Whoa!

01:09:14.100 --> 01:09:15.580
Whoa!

01:09:15.580 --> 01:09:17.090
I'll be needed on the bridge.

01:09:17.090 --> 01:09:18.990
If you keep this up, you're going to regret it

01:09:18.990 --> 01:09:20.190
for the rest of your life.

01:09:20.190 --> 01:09:21.650
I thought you'd welcome the opportunity

01:09:21.650 --> 01:09:24.850
to settle your score with Sha, but I guess I overestimated you.

01:09:24.850 --> 01:09:26.680
Come on, Frau Bo.

01:09:26.680 --> 01:09:27.630
Sha?

01:09:27.630 --> 01:09:28.250
Huh?

01:09:28.250 --> 01:09:30.000
Hey, Noah, wait!

01:09:30.380 --> 01:09:30.780
Noah!

01:09:31.550 --> 01:09:32.460
Amuro, listen.

01:09:32.820 --> 01:09:35.820
You have the operator's instruction manual for using the Gundam, don't you?

01:09:36.150 --> 01:09:36.430
Hmm?

01:09:36.630 --> 01:09:37.950
Let me borrow it for a little while.

