01:51:36.230 --> 01:51:37.170
Why should I?

01:51:37.170 --> 01:51:38.170
I don't give a hoot.

01:51:38.170 --> 01:51:41.700
He might cause trouble for others, but not for me.

01:51:41.700 --> 01:51:47.730
Might as well check him out, but it's a white-based problem, not mine.

01:51:47.730 --> 01:51:58.490
I was afraid they weren't gonna make it!

01:51:58.490 --> 01:52:00.000
Get the emergency crew out there!

01:52:01.340 --> 01:52:03.300
Oh no, this is a major base!

01:52:03.300 --> 01:52:12.680
Steady! Gotta do better than that!

01:52:12.680 --> 01:52:25.510
At it!

01:52:25.510 --> 01:52:28.450
Hey! The Medea! Of course!

01:52:28.450 --> 01:52:30.000
They're coming to fly cover for us!

01:52:30.890 --> 01:52:42.710
what rotten luck they didn't realize their rendezvous point was so near a

01:52:42.710 --> 01:52:59.430
major enemy base if I had raised him he wouldn't have turned out this way he was

01:52:59.430 --> 01:53:00.000
so gentle

01:53:00.000 --> 01:53:01.260
he wouldn't have heard a fly.

01:53:03.770 --> 01:53:05.490
What have they done to my poor Amuro?

01:53:07.650 --> 01:53:22.180
That ammunition we could have captured.

01:53:22.890 --> 01:53:25.470
Pearson, order all of our fighters to pull out of there now.

01:53:25.830 --> 01:53:26.130
Radio.

01:53:26.370 --> 01:53:26.590
Right.

01:53:30.700 --> 01:53:34.260
You're destroying precious supplies. Pull out of there immediately.

01:53:34.260 --> 01:53:37.650
Follow us. We'll keep you covered.

01:53:37.650 --> 01:53:39.090
We're retreating?

01:53:39.090 --> 01:53:44.560
Is there somewhere we can take white base for repairs?

01:53:44.560 --> 01:53:46.260
And what do we do with all those civilians?

01:53:46.260 --> 01:53:49.660
I'll set up a new rendezvous at Point W, 200 clicks north of here.

01:53:49.660 --> 01:53:52.760
And don't ask me what I want to do with the damn civilians.

01:54:05.020 --> 01:54:07.260
So does this mean you don't want to stay here with me?

01:54:07.610 --> 01:54:11.570
I wish I could, but I have a greater responsibility to all my friends aboard that ship.

01:54:15.420 --> 01:54:20.900
It's a real honor to meet Amaro's mother.

01:54:21.280 --> 01:54:23.950
I appreciate you having taken such good care of him.

01:54:24.280 --> 01:54:28.010
I don't exaggerate when I say we all owe our lives to your heroic son, madam.

01:54:28.300 --> 01:54:30.000
Did you say heroic? Amaro?

01:54:30.600 --> 01:54:34.900
He has served well above the call of duty, and you have every reason to be very proud of your son.

01:54:35.100 --> 01:54:36.680
How kind of you to say so.

01:54:37.010 --> 01:54:39.290
So, we have to launch right away.

01:54:40.200 --> 01:54:42.220
Have you decided what you're going to do, Amara?

01:54:42.240 --> 01:54:42.900
Yes, I have.

01:54:44.820 --> 01:54:45.300
What?

01:54:46.310 --> 01:54:47.670
Goodbye.

01:54:48.130 --> 01:54:48.930
But I...

01:54:48.930 --> 01:54:49.730
Stay well, Mother.

01:54:50.270 --> 01:54:51.280
Please write to me.

01:54:51.770 --> 01:54:52.490
I'll write back.

01:54:55.800 --> 01:54:58.320
Be assured, I'll watch after him like a brother.

01:55:18.720 --> 01:55:26.720
*crying*

01:56:06.200 --> 01:56:07.200
All clear ahead, sir.

01:56:07.860 --> 01:56:09.320
Rendezvous point W, sailor.

01:56:41.070 --> 01:56:42.990
We should have the engine repairs done by sunup.

01:56:43.850 --> 01:56:45.350
Well, I have a few minutes free now.

01:56:45.570 --> 01:56:46.950
You said you had some questions for me?

01:56:47.770 --> 01:56:50.250
For one thing, I'm wondering why you haven't given my crew

01:56:50.250 --> 01:56:51.330
any training discipline.

01:56:51.610 --> 01:56:53.830
According to every evaluation I've heard or read,

01:56:53.930 --> 01:56:55.370
the performance of the white-based crew

01:56:55.370 --> 01:56:57.930
has exceeded all expectations we'd ever hoped for.

01:56:58.470 --> 01:57:00.000
The top brass have decided

01:57:00.000 --> 01:57:04.420
to keep the ship under your command your first assignment is in Europe where we're launching

01:57:04.420 --> 01:57:08.660
a major new offensive at the same time we'll investigate all these rumors we keep hearing

01:57:08.660 --> 01:57:15.800
about new types what are new types I haven't heard the rumors you will they're they're

01:57:15.800 --> 01:57:20.640
like super espers they have fantastic mental energies and powers of intuition so incredible

01:57:20.640 --> 01:57:25.080
that many people are tempted to believe they're supernatural hmm if only we had a few people

01:57:25.080 --> 01:57:30.000
like that working with us we could get rid of the Zeons in no time at all by the way congratulations

01:57:30.000 --> 01:57:31.750
Congratulations, Lieutenant J.G.

01:57:31.830 --> 01:57:34.000
Huh? Is that a... promotion?

01:57:35.110 --> 01:57:37.110
I'm a... what? What's the matter, Amuro?

01:57:37.540 --> 01:57:39.370
Huh? Matter? What do you mean?

01:57:39.650 --> 01:57:42.430
You ought to be sleeping. It's well past your bedtime, kid.

01:57:42.470 --> 01:57:43.350
Yeah, right.

01:57:43.650 --> 01:57:43.990
Amuro?

01:57:44.620 --> 01:57:44.980
Yes?

01:57:46.950 --> 01:57:48.770
Being a pilot is a big responsibility.

01:57:49.310 --> 01:57:51.630
Part of your job is getting a healthy amount of rest.

01:57:51.850 --> 01:57:52.970
I will. Thank you.

01:57:54.830 --> 01:57:55.410
Good night, ma'am.

01:57:55.670 --> 01:57:57.050
Good night, Lieutenant J.G.

01:57:57.050 --> 01:57:57.330
Good night.

01:58:02.840 --> 01:58:04.520
I came by to see you. Where were you?

01:58:04.520 --> 01:58:06.120
I stepped out to the lounge for a minute.

01:58:06.120 --> 01:58:08.360
The lounge is that way, Amuro.

01:58:08.360 --> 01:58:13.160
All right, so what?

01:58:13.160 --> 01:58:16.030
What's wrong with you?

01:58:16.030 --> 01:58:17.380
Nothing's wrong.

01:58:17.380 --> 01:58:19.180
Good night, Amuro. Sleep well.

01:58:19.180 --> 01:58:22.340
Let's go, Haro.

01:58:22.340 --> 01:58:24.100
What's with her?

01:58:57.870 --> 01:58:59.960
Good to see you. I hope you had breakfast.

01:59:02.490 --> 01:59:07.510
Amuro have you had breakfast yet no sir, but not yet sir do it now

01:59:07.510 --> 01:59:09.510
We're going to be flying through Zeon territory

01:59:10.030 --> 01:59:27.010
Gundam will be on combat alert. I will right away sir escape route sir, and here's white faces route

01:59:27.010 --> 01:59:30.000
We currently project a blanket all clear for both of these courses

01:59:30.090 --> 01:59:32.330
We'll be safer flying over the ocean on our way to Europe.

01:59:32.330 --> 01:59:34.040
Oh, that's right. Launch!

01:59:34.040 --> 01:59:51.920
I don't want people to laugh at me or say I was made an admiral just because I'm your son.

01:59:51.920 --> 01:59:56.710
That's why I don't plan to return to Zeon until after I have achieved a triumphant victory.

01:59:56.710 --> 01:59:59.570
Then there will be no room for doubt in anyone's mind.

02:00:00.000 --> 02:00:02.640
and I want you to have real reason to be proud of me, Father.

02:00:03.840 --> 02:00:06.920
I look forward to the opportunity of proving my worthiness.

02:00:07.700 --> 02:00:17.850
You mustn't let your grief cause you to neglect your duties.

02:00:19.630 --> 02:00:22.330
I hope you can forgive me for speaking so boldly, Highness.

02:00:22.890 --> 02:00:24.600
But it's important that you make an appearance.

02:00:25.550 --> 02:00:27.130
Your people need to see their...

02:00:27.130 --> 02:00:27.990
Very well, Kish.

02:01:11.520 --> 02:01:13.620
Cramp, what's everybody so excited about?

02:01:13.620 --> 02:01:17.620
We've located an unidentified ship of a type I've never seen before.

02:01:17.620 --> 02:01:18.820
Okay, bring it up.

02:01:18.820 --> 02:01:23.270
Is that the Trojan horse, sir?

02:01:23.270 --> 02:01:27.010
Romba, could it be we'll have the opportunity of avenging Master Garma?

02:01:27.010 --> 02:01:28.770
Let's not be so hasty, Hummel.

02:01:30.250 --> 02:01:33.750
We've just begun re-entry, so we're helpless to do anything.

02:01:33.750 --> 02:01:36.770
And we're too far from the base to call fighters out here in time.

02:01:36.770 --> 02:01:40.590
After we clear re-entry, we can launch Zanzibar, but we have no fighter backup, just re-entry

02:01:40.590 --> 02:01:42.880
capsules.

02:01:42.880 --> 02:01:45.280
We need fighters.

02:01:45.280 --> 02:01:48.750
So exactly what are we going to do, just let them get away?

02:01:48.750 --> 02:01:51.990
I have standing orders to avenge the son of Daejin.

02:01:51.990 --> 02:01:56.200
And when you receive a direct order from an admiral, it is not to be taken lightly.

02:01:56.200 --> 02:02:00.000
You'll have time to make plans while we're in re-entry, and I have every confidence you'll

02:02:00.000 --> 02:02:00.800
think of something, sir.

02:02:00.800 --> 02:02:03.260
I sincerely appreciate your vote of confidence, Haman.

02:02:03.440 --> 02:02:05.420
I only wish I felt similar assurance.

02:02:13.330 --> 02:02:25.940
Are you still doing repair work?

02:02:26.060 --> 02:02:26.340
Yeah.

02:02:27.280 --> 02:02:29.110
You don't look well, Amuro.

02:02:29.290 --> 02:02:30.000
What's wrong?

02:02:30.060 --> 02:02:35.550
nothing's wrong haro what are you working on computer unit don't forget to eat your dinner

02:02:35.550 --> 02:02:43.010
before it gets cold right right i'm a rope your brainwave readings have fallen distressingly low

02:02:43.010 --> 02:02:52.210
i'm all right come on haro he doesn't want to be bothered i'll return later to pick up

02:02:52.210 --> 02:03:00.000
the dishes don't wear yourself out i think that just about does it yeah now then i'll

02:03:00.030 --> 02:03:01.510
I guess I better go eat dinner.

02:03:30.060 --> 02:03:32.200
Kieran, I haven't seen Shaw. Where is he?

02:03:32.660 --> 02:03:36.650
I would imagine Shaw has rejoined his unit, wherever that is.

02:03:37.060 --> 02:03:37.800
I see.

02:03:46.130 --> 02:03:47.050
Yes, at once.

02:03:59.520 --> 02:04:00.000
Intensify!

02:04:00.000 --> 02:04:01.000
I port-side fire!

02:04:01.000 --> 02:04:02.000
Pardon me, sir.

02:04:02.000 --> 02:04:03.890
Shall I take evasive maneuvers?

02:04:03.890 --> 02:04:05.890
We might be able to hide in those clouds to starboard.

02:04:05.890 --> 02:04:07.810
That storm looks like a bad one.

02:04:07.810 --> 02:04:11.900
It is a bad one.

02:04:11.900 --> 02:04:15.550
Looks like the end of the world.

02:04:15.550 --> 02:04:16.550
What happened?

02:04:16.550 --> 02:04:17.550
Don't worry.

02:04:17.550 --> 02:04:18.550
The Gundam will protect us.

02:04:18.550 --> 02:04:23.000
You have to admit, it's pretty scary.

02:04:23.000 --> 02:04:25.000
Maybe the Zeons have a new kind of ray gun.

02:04:25.000 --> 02:04:30.000
It looks like the Feddies are using a new secret weapon.

02:04:30.000 --> 02:04:35.720
sir no it's a natural phenomenon on earth they call it lightning there's

02:04:35.720 --> 02:04:40.410
really no cause for alarm I've seen this often on my trips to earth don't fret

02:04:40.410 --> 02:04:46.810
about any danger just try to appreciate the beauty of it all we're hidden from

02:04:46.810 --> 02:04:52.210
sight look for a place to bring us down yes sir scan the surface immediately

02:04:52.210 --> 02:04:56.710
with infrared sensors check the terrain with a laser scan as well marker confirm

02:04:56.710 --> 02:04:58.360
our heading and entry angle

02:05:01.370 --> 02:05:04.370
That's going to be a tight squeeze with no margin for error, Mirai.

02:05:04.370 --> 02:05:05.370
Think you can handle it?

02:05:05.370 --> 02:05:06.370
Yes, sir.

02:05:06.370 --> 02:05:24.100
We have now come to zero speed, sir.

02:05:24.100 --> 02:05:25.500
Well done, Mirai.

02:05:25.500 --> 02:05:26.400
I'm impressed.

02:05:26.400 --> 02:05:28.470
Now then, attention all sections.

02:05:28.470 --> 02:05:30.000
Activate anti-aircraft batteries.

02:05:30.000 --> 02:05:34.470
at once. Mobile suits prepare for launch. Amaro, are you still here lying around and

02:05:34.470 --> 02:05:45.420
moping? What am I gonna do with him? Hurry! We gotta go! Come on, snap out of it, Amaro.

02:05:45.420 --> 02:05:49.430
I'm not gonna let you give in at this thing. Hey! Leave me alone. Listen! Come off it.

02:05:49.430 --> 02:05:52.310
You're endangering yourself and a lot of others acting this way. Mind your own

02:05:52.310 --> 02:05:59.760
business, Rio. No more fooling around. Alright, let go. You can be persuasive when you want.

02:06:01.370 --> 02:06:09.980
there they go let's hope they didn't spot us yeah that was them all right right the magnetic

02:06:09.980 --> 02:06:17.340
signature topped off the scale notify fw with a signal flare trojan horse sat down and is hiding

02:06:17.340 --> 02:06:21.500
on land sir we pinpointed their location with magno scan transmit the coordinates to our

02:06:21.500 --> 02:06:30.000
computer at once yes sir stand by to set a new course enemy closing launch cover fire

02:06:30.280 --> 02:06:34.140
Give us a missile umbrella and prepare a gun dam and gun cannon for a quick launch on my command.

02:06:37.950 --> 02:06:44.560
Last, we have the elusive Trojan horse inside our scanner range.

02:06:44.680 --> 02:06:45.640
Start collecting data.

02:06:49.600 --> 02:06:54.040
This is how I always want to remember you.

02:06:54.390 --> 02:06:58.620
It's such a thrill to see you charging into battle personally instead of just giving orders.

02:06:58.620 --> 02:06:59.760
Hmm.

02:07:00.000 --> 02:07:05.490
This is something I have to handle personally, there's too much riding on it.

02:07:05.490 --> 02:07:06.990
Nobody but my team goes in.

02:07:06.990 --> 02:07:08.300
A goose!

02:07:08.300 --> 02:07:09.300
Cousin!

02:07:09.300 --> 02:07:10.700
Ready to launch, sir.

02:07:10.700 --> 02:07:17.540
Ready, sir!

02:07:17.540 --> 02:07:19.840
We're concentrating our attention on the Trojan horse.

02:07:19.840 --> 02:07:22.820
They'll no doubt send their mobile suits out to lure us away.

02:07:22.820 --> 02:07:24.510
Don't let that kind of trickery take you in.

02:07:24.510 --> 02:07:25.510
Yes, sir!

02:07:25.510 --> 02:07:26.510
Are we cleared for launch?

02:07:26.510 --> 02:07:28.510
Launch bay doors are opening now.

02:07:28.510 --> 02:07:30.000
Their mobile suits are no match for us.

02:07:30.250 --> 02:07:31.550
Just knock them out of your way.

02:07:33.430 --> 02:07:49.150
We've held them down as long as we could, but we're hopelessly outgunned,

02:07:49.170 --> 02:07:50.510
and I need to get my men out of here.

02:07:50.730 --> 02:07:51.970
Request permission to withdraw.

02:07:52.570 --> 02:07:54.370
Well done. Return to base immediately.

02:07:54.650 --> 02:07:56.730
Lieutenant Ranba will be taking over from here.

02:07:56.910 --> 02:07:58.880
Attack wing, disengage, and return to base.

02:07:58.880 --> 02:07:59.060
Okay.

02:08:00.540 --> 02:08:03.320
Lieutenant Bright, look at that, those commasides pulled out.

02:08:03.400 --> 02:08:06.100
Now's our chance to execute our escape plan. Stand by.

02:08:07.670 --> 02:08:09.930
Ryu, are you and Amuro standing by for a launch?

02:08:09.950 --> 02:08:10.250
Negative.

02:08:10.780 --> 02:08:11.360
What do you mean?

02:08:11.520 --> 02:08:15.300
Amuro's emotionally exhausted, Lieutenant Bright. He's walking around like some kind of zombie.

02:08:15.460 --> 02:08:20.100
I won't have it. He can have his breakdown some other day. I want him ready to launch right now.

02:08:20.120 --> 02:08:21.980
I'll try and wake him up, but it won't be easy.

02:08:22.660 --> 02:08:24.510
Come on, Amuro. Time to go to work.

02:08:25.150 --> 02:08:28.310
I'll just have to leave it up to you, whether to launch or not. I have to get out there.

02:08:28.530 --> 02:08:28.930
Grrrr!

02:08:32.040 --> 02:08:35.140
Amuro, I sure hope you're ready because we have you locked into the Catapult.

02:08:35.430 --> 02:08:36.590
Please tell me that you're awake.

02:08:36.790 --> 02:08:38.610
You can go ahead and launch me, Sailor. I'm ready.

02:08:39.040 --> 02:08:40.700
You don't sound alert. What's wrong?

02:08:41.150 --> 02:08:43.130
I'm awake now. I'm on my way, Ryo.

02:08:43.450 --> 02:08:46.170
Maybe a bit of action will bring Amuro back to life, Sailor.

02:08:46.290 --> 02:08:48.700
Very well. Gundam is now clear for launching.

02:09:13.280 --> 02:09:14.920
Cover fire. Blanket that hillside.

02:09:16.930 --> 02:09:19.030
All right. You've had it.

02:09:19.240 --> 02:09:20.660
You made the mistake of making me mad.

02:09:22.790 --> 02:09:25.770
Wake now.

02:09:30.700 --> 02:09:32.530
Akus! Toss out a cracker!

02:09:35.300 --> 02:09:37.300
Oh no! Now what?

02:09:37.300 --> 02:09:51.110
Take his rifle away!

02:09:53.140 --> 02:09:55.330
Oh no!

02:10:05.400 --> 02:10:10.260
Watch it.

02:10:10.260 --> 02:10:11.500
Thanks.

02:10:11.500 --> 02:10:14.700
And now it looks like they're launching a third one.

02:10:14.700 --> 02:10:15.700
Gotta move on, Hayato.

02:10:15.700 --> 02:10:17.700
Amaro's going hand-to-hand with three of them.

02:10:17.700 --> 02:10:18.700
Give him cover fire, quick!

02:10:18.700 --> 02:10:28.450
You guys developed some new secret weapons, too.

02:10:28.450 --> 02:10:30.000
Gundam's ready for you.

02:10:31.340 --> 02:10:35.790
to expect from these guys. Amro, be careful!

02:10:35.790 --> 02:10:43.400
Huh?

02:10:43.400 --> 02:10:55.660
A laser sword?

02:10:55.660 --> 02:10:58.550
Take the advantage when you've got it, or end up dead.

02:11:03.900 --> 02:11:08.240
Oh, man. That new Zaku has more power and heavier weapons than we ever suspected.

02:11:14.720 --> 02:11:17.280
Hakus! Kuzun! Disengage! We're going back to the ship!

02:11:39.560 --> 02:11:41.420
- All aboard and standing by.

02:11:41.420 --> 02:11:42.900
- Blast out of here immediately.

02:11:42.900 --> 02:11:44.620
Full power, evasive maneuvering,

02:11:44.620 --> 02:11:46.620
and throw out the blinders to cover our retreat.

02:11:46.620 --> 02:11:56.180
- I can't see anything.

02:12:27.550 --> 02:12:28.550
Why did they run away?

02:12:30.000 --> 02:12:34.070
know whether they gave up or if they just let us get away this is both a

02:12:34.070 --> 02:12:38.940
tragic occasion and one of profound inspiration for all zeons I have lost a

02:12:38.940 --> 02:12:43.330
brother and our people have lost a great hero but we shall not surrender to our

02:12:43.330 --> 02:12:48.190
grief we shall draw on his example and continue fighting on to avenge all our

02:12:48.190 --> 02:12:52.170
fallen loved ones we will endure these sacrifices and we will build our nation

02:12:52.170 --> 02:13:00.000
ever stronger don't give up how is it that they're broadcasting Garma's memorial ceremony on

02:13:00.000 --> 02:13:05.470
worldwide network and he's using it for propaganda of course cause it's just for

02:13:05.470 --> 02:13:09.030
50 years a greedy clique of the elite have extended the earth Federation's

02:13:09.030 --> 02:13:13.450
brutal control of space at our expense we were forced to leave our beloved

02:13:13.450 --> 02:13:17.850
planet Earth in order to form space colonies for the Federation and how many

02:13:17.850 --> 02:13:21.330
times since then is the Federation turned a deaf ear to our pleas for

02:13:21.330 --> 02:13:26.080
freedom independence and equality but we no longer plead for our rights we

02:13:26.080 --> 02:13:30.000
demand them my beloved brother Garma gave his life to this

02:13:30.860 --> 02:13:32.000
He was eager to die.

02:13:32.280 --> 02:13:35.060
All of us must dedicate ourselves to winning this war.

02:13:35.720 --> 02:13:38.600
Hardships of living in space have served to prepare us well.

02:13:39.300 --> 02:13:39.740
Bartender.

02:13:40.080 --> 02:13:42.620
Allow me the honor of buying you that drink, young man.

02:13:43.180 --> 02:13:44.840
Ah, how did I join you?

02:13:45.120 --> 02:13:46.440
Thank you very much.

02:13:46.980 --> 02:13:50.500
Well, sir, let me guess, you're with the Royal Guard, right?

02:13:51.840 --> 02:13:53.040
Is it that obvious?

02:13:53.540 --> 02:13:54.620
One of Kashiri's men.

02:13:55.360 --> 02:13:57.360
Very good, Commander, you have a sharp eye.

02:13:57.360 --> 02:14:00.000
We destroy us, our culture, and it traces us.

02:14:00.000 --> 02:14:02.000
Are you sure you're all right now, Amaro?

02:14:02.000 --> 02:14:05.000
I realize I caused you a lot of worry. I'm sorry about that.

02:14:05.000 --> 02:14:06.000
I understand.

02:14:06.000 --> 02:14:08.460
